hes across the two files (same date/teams/score). novo dates are DD/MM/YYYY, Brasileirao has datetime. Same match: Flamengo vs Vasco on same date with same score. Dedup by (date, home_key, away_key, home_goals, away_goals). The two files should contain the same matches for 2012-2019 — after dedup, one copy each. But subtle differences (e.g., round numbers, or matches recorded with slight date differences) could cause dupes. Let me check overlap: novo 2012-2019 has ~380 matches/season × 8 = 3040. Brasileirao 2012-2022: 4180 over 11 seasons ≈ 380/season × 11 = 4180. Yes both are complete seasons for 2012-2019.\n    \n    Dedup approach: for each (competition, season), if multiple sources provide matches, prefer the more authoritative source. I'll implement dedup keyed on (date, home_entity, away_entity, home_goals, away_goals, competition-canonical). This should collapse 2012-2019 overlap. Any matches that don't dedupe exactly (date format issues etc.) would remain duplicated — need to verify standings results are sane (e.g., 2019 champion = Flamengo, 2018 = Palmeiras — known facts I can assert in tests!).\n\n    Actually wait — do novo and Brasileirao_Matches have the same dates? novo \"29/03/2003\" (date only) and Brasileirao \"2012-05-19 18:30:00\". For overlapping matches, date parts should match. I'll normalize to date objects. Round numbers might differ slightly, but dedup on date+teams+score is robust.\n    \n    Also BR-Football \"Serie A\" (3689 matches) overlaps too! Serie A in BR-Football covers which seasons? 3689 matches... 2012-2019 from its Copa do Brasil date range 2023? First rows are 2023 Copa do Brasil. Let me check BR-Football Serie A seasons and whether they overlap with the others. 3689 / 380 ≈ 9.7 seasons. Need to check. If BR-Football Serie A covers e.g. 2014-2023, there's triple overlap for some seasons.\n    \n    And BR-Football \"Copa do Brasil\" (1123) overlaps Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv (1337, 2012-2021). Brazilian Cup has rounds as number