search_matches, return all (or dedup by default with option `include_duplicates`)? Simpler: search_matches returns deduped by default (cleaner answers). I'll expose `include_all_sources` param.\n    \n    For extended stats (corners etc.), keep them on the match record when the source is BR-Football; dedup preference... If I prefer Brasileirao_Matches for Serie A 2012-2019, then BR-Football's corners for those matches are lost. If I prefer BR-Football, I lose round numbers. Which matters more? Standings need round? No — standings need season results only. Match listing shows \"Round 22\" nicely. Extended stats enable \"corners\" queries — not explicitly required by spec (\"Various skill ratings\" is FIFA; corners not in required capabilities). Required: date, scores, competition for match listing; W/L/D; goals.\n    \n    Plan: dedup with preference Brasileirao_Matches first, then novo, then Cup file, then Libertadores, then BR-Football last. But MERGE extended stats: when a BR-Football duplicate matches (same date/teams/score/competition), attach its corner/shot/attack stats to the kept record. Nice — best of both.\n    \n    Wait, but do Brasileirao and BR-Football Serie A matches share the same dates? BR-Football date \"2023-09-24\" style. Should match. And same score. Risk: BR-Football team names unaccented (\"Sao Paulo\") — normalization handles. One more risk: goal types — BR-Football has floats \"1.0\" → int(1.0)=1 fine.\n\n    For standings: compute from deduped matches of competition \"Brasileirão Serie A\" per season. For 2003-2011 from novo only. 2012-2019 from Brasileirao(+novo dedup). 2020-2022 from Brasileirao only. Wait, BR-Football Serie A might cover 2023! Brasileirao_Matches ends 2022. If BR-Football covers 2023 Serie A, that's unique data. 3689 matches... let me check its season range. I'll check in exploration.\n\n    Sanity checks with known facts:\n    - 2019 Brasileirão champion: Flamengo (90 pts? they had 90). \n    - 2018: Palmeiras (80 pts)