lves carry qualifiers → re-split.\n\nDate parsing:\n\n```python\n_DATE_FORMATS = (\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\", \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M\", \"%Y-%m-%d\", \"%d/%m/%Y %H:%M\", \"%d/%m/%Y\")\n\ndef parse_date(value) -> tuple[date | None, str | None]:\n    # returns (date, hh:mm) \n```\nTry each format with datetime.strptime; on \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\" extract time. Actually simpler: try full datetime formats first, extract .date() and .time(); then date-only.\n\nparse_goals(value) -> int | None: handle \"\", \"NA\", \"-\", \"None\", floats \"1.0\", ints, numeric strings.\n\nparse_int similar.\n\n**models.py**:\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass Match:\n    date: date\n    time: str | None\n    competition: str\n    season: int\n    home_team: str          # entity id\n    away_team: str\n    home_display: str\n    away_display: str\n    home_goals: int\n    away_goals: int\n    round: int | None = None\n    stage: str | None = None\n    stadium: str | None = None\n    source: str = \"\"\n    # extended stats\n    home_corners: ... = None\n    ...\n    @property winner: str | None -> entity id? or \"home\"/\"away\"/None (draw) — compute via goals.\n    def to_dict(...)\n    @property sort_key\n```\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass TeamEntity:\n    key: str\n    display: str\n    variants: list[str]\n    qualifiers: set[str]\n    def to_dict(...)\n```\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass Player:\n    fifa_id: int\n    name: str\n    age: int|None\n    nationality: str\n    overall: int|None\n    potential: int|None\n    club: str\n    club_key: str      # entity id or normalized club string\n    position: str|None\n    position_group: str\n    jersey: int|None\n    height: str; weight: str; foot; value; wage\n    attributes: dict[str,str]\n    def to_dict(core=False)\n```\n\n**repository.py**: \n\n```python\nDATA_FILES = {...}\nCOMPETITION_ALIASES = {\n    \"brasileirao\": \"Brasileirão Serie A\", \"serie a\": ..., \"campeonato brasileiro\": ...,\n    \"serie b\": \"Brasileirão Serie B\", \"serie 