elf._entities.values() if e.key == q_base or e.key.startswith(q_base + \" \")]\n    if same_base: return sorted(...)\n    # 3. substring fallback over variants/keys (typos, partial names)\n    sub = [e for e in ... if q_base in e.key]  # + variant bases contain?\n    return sorted(sub)\n```\n\nCareful: \"atletico\" → step 2 returns 3 entities (atletico mg/go/pr...). Tools receiving multiple → either aggregate (search_matches: use ALL) or error with disambiguation (team_stats, head_to_head). I'll make search_matches accept multiple (matches any of them); team_stats aggregate across them? Hmm — \"What is Atletico's record?\" ambiguous → better to error listing. But for search_matches \"atletico matches\" → return matches for all three with note. OK: per-tool policy.\n\nAlso \"america\" → 2 entities. \"botafogo\" alias→\"botafogo rj\" directly (alias in FULL_NAME_ALIASES: \"botafogo\" → \"botafogo rj\"). Wait — that alias makes bare \"Botafogo\" always RJ. In match data bare \"Botafogo\"... BR-Football? Let me check \"Botafogo\" bare in BR-Football — earlier I saw 'Botafogo' in FIFA; BR-Football 'Botafogo PB'. If BR-Football also has bare \"Botafogo\" it's the RJ club (Serie A/B context). Aliased ✓. And \"Botafogo-RJ\" → base \"botafogo\" qual \"rj\" → entity \"botafogo rj\" ✓ same.\n\nHmm, wait — the FULL_NAME_ALIASES are applied to the DE-QUALIFIED base. \"botafogo rj\" (from Botafogo-RJ) → base \"botafogo\" qual \"rj\" → base not in aliases (key \"botafogo\" IS in aliases → maps to \"botafogo rj\" → re-split → base \"botafogo\" qual \"rj\" ✓ consistent loop, no infinite recursion since alias target re-splits to same (base,qual). But \"botafogo pb\" → base \"botafogo\" → alias \"botafogo\"→\"botafogo rj\"?? WAIT NO. The alias applies to the BASE after removing the qualifier — so \"Botafogo-PB\" → base \"botafogo\" → alias → \"botafogo rj\" → WRONG! It'd turn the Paraíba club into RJ club!!\n\nI must apply bare-name aliases ONLY when no qualifier was present. Design: 