{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788237549225,"sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a77ea6de8a1ad362","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"Data models shared across the Brazilian soccer MCP server.\n\nContext: the repository layer loads ~42k raw CSV rows into these plain\ndataclasses once at startup; every MCP tool answers questions by filtering\nand aggregating in-memory instances. Matches carry resolved team entity\nids plus the original display spellings, players carry both the raw FIFA\nrow and a normalised club key so that player and match data can be joined\nacross files.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom datetime import date\n\nPOSITION_GROUPS = {\n    \"GK\": \"goalkeeper\",\n    \"LB\": \"defender\", \"LWB\": \"defender\", \"RB\": \"defender\", \"RWB\": \"defender\",\n    \"CB\": \"defender\", \"LCB\": \"defender\", \"RCB\": \"defender\",\n    \"CDM\": \"midfielder\", \"LDM\": \"midfielder\", \"RDM\": \"midfielder\",\n    \"CM\": \"midfielder\", \"LCM\": \"midfielder\", \"RCM\": \"midfielder\",\n    \"CAM\": \"midfielder\", \"LAM\": \"midfielder\", \"RAM\": \"midfielder\",\n    \"LM\": \"midfielder\", \"RM\": \"midfielder\",\n    \"LW\": \"forward\", \"RW\": \"forward\", \"LF\": \"forward\", \"RF\": \"forward\",\n    \"LS\": \"forward\", \"RS\": \"forward\", \"ST\": \"forward\", \"CF\": \"forward\",\n}\n\nLIBERTADORES_STAGE_ORDER = {\n    \"group stage\": 0,\n    \"round of 16\": 1,\n    \"quarterfinals\": 2,\n    \"semifinals\": 3,\n    \"final\": 4,\n}\n\n\ndef position_group(position: str | None) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Map a FIFA position code to goalkeeper/defender/midfielder/forward.\"\"\"\n    if not position:\n        return \"unknown\"\n    return POSITION_GROUPS.get(position.strip().upper(), \"unknown\")\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Match:\n    \"\"\"One played match, normalised across the six source files.\"\"\"\n\n    date: date\n    competition: str\n    season: int\n    home_team: str\n    away_team: str\n    home_display: str\n    away_display: str\n    home_goals: int\n    away_goals: int\n    time: str | None = None\n    round: int | None = None\n    stage: str | None = None\n    stadium: str | None = None\n    source: str = \"\"\n    home_corners: int | None = None\n    away_corners: int | None = None\n    home_shots: int | None = None\n    away_shots: int | None = None\n    home_attacks: int | None = None\n    away_attacks: int | None = None\n    home_ht_goals: int | None = None\n    away_ht_goals: int | None = None\n\n    @property\n    def outcome(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Return \"home\", \"away\" or \"draw\" for the match result.\"\"\"\n        if self.home_goals > self.away_goals:\n            return \"home\"\n        if self.away_goals > self.home_goals:\n            return \"away\"\n        return \"draw\"\n\n    @property\n    def stage_order(self) -> int:\n        return LIBERTADORES_STAGE_ORDER.get(self.stage or \"\", 99)\n\n    @property\n    def sort_key(self):\n        return (self.date, self.time or \"\", self.competition, self.stage_order)\n\n    @property\n    def margin(self) -> int:\n        return abs(self.home_goals - self.away_goals)\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        payload = {\n            \"date\": self.date.isoformat(),\n            \"time\": self.time,\n            \"competition\": self.competition,\n            \"season\": self.season,\n            \"home_team\": self.home_display,\n            \"away_team\": self.away_display,\n            \"home_goals\": self.home_goals,\n            \"away_goals\": self.away_goals,\n            \"round\": self.round,\n            \"stage\": self.stage,\n            \"stadium\": self.stadium,\n            \"source\": self.source,\n        }\n        extras = {\n            \"home_corners\": self.home_corners,\n            \"away_corners\": self.away_corners,\n            \"home_shots\": self.home_shots,\n            \"away_shots\": self.away_shots,\n            \"home_attacks\": self.home_attacks,\n            \"away_attacks\": self.away_attacks,\n        }\n        payload.update({k: v for k, v in extras.items() if v is not None})\n        return payload\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass TeamEntity:\n    \"\"\"A real-world club resolved from all of its spelling variants.\"\"\"\n\n    key: str\n    display: str\n    variants: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n    qualifiers: set = field(default_factory=set)\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        return {\n            \"team\": self.display,\n            \"key\": self.key,\n            \"also_seen_as\": self.variants[:8],\n        }\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Player:\n    \"\"\"One row of the FIFA player database.\"\"\"\n\n    fifa_id: int\n    name: str\n    age: int | None\n    nationality: str\n    overall: int | None\n    potential: int | None\n    club: str\n    club_key: str\n    position: str | None\n    position_group: str\n    jersey: int | None\n    height: str | None\n    weight: str | None\n    preferred_foot: str | None\n    value: str | None\n    wage: str | None\n    attributes: dict = field(default_factory=dict)\n\n    def to_dict(self, detailed: bool = False) -> dict:\n        payload = {\n            \"id\": self.fifa_id,\n            \"name\": self.name,\n            \"age\": self.age,\n            \"nationality\": self.nationality,\n            \"overall\": self.overall,\n            \"potential\": self.potential,\n            \"club\": self.club,\n            \"position\": self.position,\n            \"position_group\": self.position_group,\n            \"jersey_number\": self.jersey,\n        }\n        if detailed:\n            payload.update(\n                {\n                    \"height\": self.height,\n                    \"weight\": self.weight,\n                    \"preferred_foot\": self.preferred_foot,\n                    \"value\": self.value,\n                    \"wage\": self.wage,\n                    \"attributes\": self.attributes,\n                }\n            )\n        return payload\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/brazilian_soccer/models.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/brazilian_soccer/models.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/models.py","time":{"start":1788237549215,"end":1788237549222}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait — I put \"vitoria\" → \"vitoria ba\" in FULL_NAME_ALIASES, but I need to double check the flow in split_team. There's a subtle issue in my split_team:\n\n```python\ncleaned = FULL_NAME_ALIASES.get(cleaned, cleaned)\nbase, qualifier = _split_qualifier(cleaned)\nbase = BASE_ALIASES.get(base, base)\nif base != cleaned and base in FULL_NAME_ALIASES:  # this condition is weird\n```\n\nHmm, that trailing block is convoluted and probably buggy. Let me trace:\n- \"Atlético-MG\" → cleaned \"atletico mg\" → not in FULL aliases → split → base \"atletico\", qual \"mg\" → BASE_ALIASES no → base == \"atletico\" != cleaned (\"atletico mg\") → check `base in FULL_NAME_ALIASES` → \"atletico\" not a key → done ✓.\n- \"Sport Club do Recife\" → cleaned \"sport club do recife\" → FULL alias → \"sport pe\" → split → base \"sport\", qual \"pe\" ✓ → BASE no → `base != cleaned` (\"sport\" != \"sport club do recife\") and \"sport\" in FULL_NAME_ALIASES? No → done ✓.\n- \"Vitória\" → cleaned \"vitoria\" → FULL alias → \"vitoria ba\" → split → base \"vitoria\", qual \"ba\" ✓ → done ✓.\n- \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" → paren → \"america fc mg\" → FULL alias? \"america fc mg\" not a key! → split → base \"america fc\", qual \"mg\" → BASE_ALIASES \"america fc\" → \"america\" ✓ → `base != cleaned` (\"america\" != \"america fc mg\") and \"america\" in FULL? NO (\"america\" isn't a key; keys are \"america fc\"...). Hmm wait — FULL has \"america fc\": \"america mg\". base is now \"america\" which is NOT in FULL → done → (\"america\", \"mg\") ✓ correct!\n- \"América FC\" (FIFA bare, no paren) → cleaned \"america fc\" → FULL alias → \"america mg\" → split → base \"america\", qual \"mg\" ✓.\n- \"Botafogo\" bare → FULL alias → \"botafogo rj\" → split → base \"botafogo\", qual \"rj\" ✓.\n- \"Botafogo-PB\" → cleaned \"botafogo pb\" → not in FULL (key is \"botafogo\" exact) → split → base \"botafogo\", qual \"pb\" → BASE_ALIASES no → `base != cleaned` and \"botafogo\" in FULL? YES → base = FULL[\"botafogo\"] = \"botafogo rj\" → split → base \"botafogo\", extra \"rj\" → qualifier = qualifier or extra = \"pb\" ✓✓ PHEW — qualifier \"pb\" preserved because `qualifier or extra` keeps existing \"pb\". \n\nHmm wait but that re-alias path is weird: base \"botafogo\" from \"Botafogo-PB\" gets re-expanded to \"botafogo rj\" then re-split to (\"botafogo\",\"rj\") but qualifier stays \"pb\" ✓. OK it works but it's fragile. When does `base in FULL_NAME_ALIASES` trigger? Only when base (de-qualified) matches a FULL key exactly. FULL keys that could be a de-qualified base: \"botafogo\" (from Botafogo-PB — handled), \"guarani\" (from Guarani-PAR!), \"vitoria\" (from Vitória-BA... wait \"Vitória-BA\" → cleaned \"vitoria ba\" — is \"vitoria ba\" in FULL? NO, key is \"vitoria\". split → base \"vitoria\" qual \"ba\" → then base != cleaned and \"vitoria\" in FULL → base = \"vitoria ba\" → split → base \"vitoria\", extra \"ba\" → qualifier = \"ba\" or \"ba\" ✓ fine).\n\n- \"Guarani-PAR\" → cleaned \"guarani par\" → not FULL key → split → base \"guarani\", qual \"par\" → `base != cleaned` and \"guarani\" in FULL → base = \"guarani sp\" → split → (\"guarani\", \"sp\") → qualifier = \"par\" or \"sp\" = \"par\" ✓ — entity \"guarani par\" ✓ correct!\n- \"Guarani\" bare (novo) → cleaned \"guarani\" → FULL → \"guarani sp\" → split → base \"guarani\" qual \"sp\" ✓.\n\nOK it works, but the logic `if base != cleaned and base in FULL_NAME_ALIASES` — the `base != cleaned` guard: when would base == cleaned AND base be a FULL key? E.g. cleaned = \"botafogo\" (bare) → first alias lookup already caught it (cleaned = FULL[\"botafogo\"]). After aliasing cleaned ≠ original... the first line `cleaned = FULL_NAME_ALIASES.get(cleaned, cleaned)` handles the full-string case. The second block handles the case where the QUALIFIER-STRIPPED base is itself an alias key (Botafogo-PB, Guarani-PAR, Vitória-BA). The `base != cleaned` guard is harmless. Actually there's a subtle infinite-recursion risk? No — single re-application, no loop.\n\nBut one flaw: for \"Vitória-BA\": cleaned \"vitoria ba\", split → base \"vitoria\" qual \"ba\"; re-alias: FULL[\"vitoria\"] = \"vitoria ba\" → split → (\"vitoria\", \"ba\") → qualifier = \"ba\" ✓. Fine.\n\nAnd \"Vitoria ES\" → base \"vitoria\" qual \"es\" → re-alias: base \"vitoria\" in FULL → \"vitoria ba\" → split → (\"vitoria\",\"ba\") → qualifier = \"es\" or \"ba\" = \"es\" ✓ → entity \"vitoria es\" ✓ correct!\n\nOK the logic works though it's subtle. Let me simplify it a bit for readability... Actually it's fine — but let me rewrite split_team more clearly to avoid the confusing re-entry:\n\n```python\ndef split_team(name):\n    cleaned = clean_text(name)\n    if not cleaned: return \"\", None\n    cleaned = FULL_NAME_ALIASES.get(cleaned, cleaned)\n    base, qualifier = _split_qualifier(cleaned)\n    base = BASE_ALIASES.get(base, base)\n    if base in FULL_NAME_ALIASES and base != cleaned:\n        expanded = FULL_NAME_ALIASES[base]\n        base, extra = _split_qualifier(expanded)\n        base = BASE_ALIASES.get(base, base)\n        qualifier = qualifier or extra\n    return base, qualifier\n```\n\nThat's what I have essentially. Hmm, `base != cleaned` — consider cleaned=\"vitoria ba\": after first get() no change (not a key). split → base \"vitoria\". \"vitoria\" in FULL ✓ and \"vitoria\" != \"vitoria ba\" ✓ → expand. Good.\n\nCons