{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788237697746,"sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9cc6d2dee686a5db","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"Data repository: loads, normalises and indexes the six Kaggle datasets.\n\nContext: three of the match files overlap heavily (e.g. the 2012-2019\nBrasileirão appears in Brasileirao_Matches.csv, novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv\nand BR-Football-Dataset.csv), teams are spelled differently in every file,\nand dates come in ISO and Brazilian formats. This module turns that pile of\nCSVs into one curated, de-duplicated in-memory match list plus a player list:\n\n* every raw team/club spelling is resolved to a TeamEntity (two spellings\n  denote the same club iff they share the same entity key),\n* for every (competition, season) exactly one source file is preferred\n  (round-by-round files first, the statistics file last), duplicate rows from\n  demoted sources are dropped, and their extended statistics (corners, shots,\n  attacks) and stadium names are merged into the kept match,\n* the FIFA player table is joined to the same team entities through the\n  normalised club key, which is what makes cross-file questions work.\n\nThe full raw match list is kept as well so that per-file queries stay\npossible (``source=`` filter on match searches).\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport csv\nimport logging\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom .models import Match, Player, TeamEntity, position_group\nfrom .normalize import (\n    clean_text,\n    is_nothing,\n    parse_date,\n    parse_int,\n    split_team,\n    strip_accents,\n)\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(\"brazilian_soccer.repository\")\n\nSERIE_A = \"Brasileirão Serie A\"\nSERIE_B = \"Brasileirão Serie B\"\nSERIE_C = \"Brasileirão Serie C\"\nCOPA_DO_BRASIL = \"Copa do Brasil\"\nLIBERTADORES = \"Copa Libertadores\"\n\nCOMPETITION_ALIASES = {\n    SERIE_A: SERIE_A,\n    SERIE_B: SERIE_B,\n    SERIE_C: SERIE_C,\n    COPA_DO_BRASIL: COPA_DO_BRASIL,\n    LIBERTADORES: LIBERTADORES,\n    \"brasileirao\": SERIE_A,\n    \"brasileirao serie a\": SERIE_A,\n    \"serie a\": SERIE_A,\n    \"campeonato brasileiro\": SERIE_A,\n    \"serie b\": SERIE_B,\n    \"brasileirao serie b\": SERIE_B,\n    \"serie c\": SERIE_C,\n    \"brasileirao serie c\": SERIE_C,\n    \"copa\": COPA_DO_BRASIL,\n    \"brazilian cup\": COPA_DO_BRASIL,\n    \"copa do brasil\": COPA_DO_BRASIL,\n    \"libertadores\": LIBERTADORES,\n    \"conmebol libertadores\": LIBERTADORES,\n    \"libertadores cup\": LIBERTADORES,\n    \"copa libertadores\": LIBERTADORES,\n}\n\nBR_FOOTBALL_TOURNAMENTS = {\n    \"Serie A\": SERIE_A,\n    \"Serie B\": SERIE_B,\n    \"Serie C\": SERIE_C,\n    \"Copa do Brasil\": COPA_DO_BRASIL,\n}\n\nSOURCE_PREFERENCE = {\n    SERIE_A: (\n        \"Brasileirao_Matches.csv\",\n        \"novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv\",\n        \"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\",\n    ),\n    SERIE_B: (\"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\",),\n    SERIE_C: (\"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\",),\n    COPA_DO_BRASIL: (\n        \"Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv\",\n        \"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\",\n    ),\n    LIBERTADORES: (\"Libertadores_Matches.csv\",),\n}\n\nDATA_FILES = (\n    \"Brasileirao_Matches.csv\",\n    \"Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv\",\n    \"Libertadores_Matches.csv\",\n    \"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\",\n    \"novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv\",\n    \"fifa_data.csv\",\n)\n\n\nclass TeamRegistry:\n    \"\"\"Resolves every spelling of a club name to a stable team entity.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        self._raw_pairs: dict[str, tuple[str, str | None]] = {}\n        self._variant_counts: dict[tuple[str, str | None], Counter] = defaultdict(Counter)\n        self._base_quals: dict[str, set] = defaultdict(set)\n        self._raw_to_key: dict[str, str] = {}\n        self.entities: dict[str, TeamEntity] = {}\n\n    def register(self, raw_name: str | None) -> None:\n        if not raw_name or is_nothing(raw_name):\n            return\n        raw_name = raw_name.strip()\n        if raw_name in self._raw_pairs:\n            return\n        pair = split_team(raw_name)\n        if not pair[0]:\n            return\n        self._raw_pairs[raw_name] = pair\n        self._variant_counts[pair][raw_name] += 0\n\n    def finalize(self) -> None:\n        for (base, qual), counter in self._variant_counts.items():\n            self._base_quals[base].add(qual)\n        for raw_name, (base, qual) in self._raw_pairs.items():\n            self._variant_counts[(base, qual)][raw_name] += 1\n            self._raw_to_key[raw_name] = self._entity_key(base, qual)\n        for (base, qual), counter in self._variant_counts.items():\n            key = self._entity_key(base, qual)\n            display = self._pick_display(key, base, counter)\n            entity = self.entities.get(key)\n            if entity is None:\n                entity = TeamEntity(key=key, display=display, variants=[])\n                self.entities[key] = entity\n            variants = [v for v, _ in counter.most_common()]\n            for variant in variants:\n                if variant not in entity.variants:\n                    entity.variants.append(variant)\n            entity.qualifiers.add(qual) if qual else entity.qualifiers.add(None)\n\n    def _entity_key(self, base: str, qual: str | None) -> str:\n        quals = {q for q in self._base_quals.get(base, set()) if q}\n        if len(quals) <= 1:\n            return base\n        return f\"{base} {qual}\" if qual else base\n\n    def _pick_display(self, key: str, base: str, counter: Counter) -> str:\n        display = counter.most_common(1)[0][0]\n        if key == base:\n            suffix = None\n            if qual := (self._base_quals.get(base) or {None}) - {None}:\n                suffix = next(iter(qual))\n            if suffix:\n                lowered = strip_accents(display).lower()\n                for token in (f\"-{suffix}\", f\" {suffix}\", f\"- {suffix}\"):\n                    if lowered.endswith(token):\n                        cut = len(display) - len(token)\n                        display = display[:cut]\n                        break\n        return display.strip() or base\n\n    def key_for(self, raw_name: str | None) -> str:\n        if not raw_name or is_nothing(raw_name):\n            return \"\"\n        return self._raw_to_key.get(raw_name.strip(), split_team(raw_name)[0])\n\n    def display_for(self, raw_name: str | None) -> str:\n        if not raw_name or is_nothing(raw_name):\n            return raw_name or \"\"\n        key = self.key_for(raw_name)\n        entity = self.entities.get(key)\n        return entity.display if entity else raw_name.strip()\n\n    def resolve(self, query: str | None) -> list[TeamEntity]:\n        \"\"\"Resolve a user-supplied team name to matching entities.\n\n        Exact matches win; otherwise all entities sharing the base name are\n        returned (e.g. \"atletico\" -> Atlético-MG, -GO and -PR); finally a\n        substring fallback catches partial spellings.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not query or is_nothing(query):\n            return []\n        base, qual = split_team(query)\n        if not base:\n            return []\n        if qual and f\"{base} {qual}\" in self.entities:\n            return [self.entities[f\"{base} {qual}\"]]\n        if base in self.entities:\n            return [self.entities[base]]\n        same_base = [e for k, e in self.entities.items() if k == base or k.startswith(base + \" \")]\n        if same_base:\n            return sorted(same_base, key=lambda e: e.key)\n        substring = [e for k, e in self.entities.items() if base in k]\n        return sorted(substring, key=lambda e: e.key)\n\n    def all_entities(self) -> list[TeamEntity]:\n        return sorted(self.entities.values(), key=lambda e: e.key)\n\n\nclass DataRepository:\n    \"\"\"Loads all datasets once and answers queries from memory.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, data_dir: str | Path | None = None) -> None:\n        if data_dir is None:\n            data_dir = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"data\" / \"kaggle\"\n        self.data_dir = Path(data_dir)\n        self.registry = TeamRegistry()\n        self.matches: list[Match] = []\n        self.raw_matches: list[Match] = []\n        self.players: list[Player] = []\n        self.load_report: dict = {}\n        self.competition_info: dict = {}\n        self.final_rounds: dict[int, int] = {}\n        self._by_entity: dict[str, list[Match]] = defaultdict(list)\n        self._load()\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------ load\n\n    def _read_csv(self, filename: str) -> list[dict]:\n        path = self.data_dir / filename\n        if not path.exists():\n            raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Required dataset file not found: {path}\")\n        with path.open(encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as handle:\n            return [row for row in csv.DictReader(handle)]\n\n    def _load(self) -> None:\n        parsed: dict[str, list[dict]] = {name: self._read_csv(name) for name in DATA_FILES}\n        rows_report: dict[str, dict] = {}\n\n        def register_file(filename: str, team_fields: tuple[str, ...]) -> None:\n            report = {\"rows\": len(parsed[filename]), \"loaded\": 0, \"skipped\": 0}\n            for row in parsed[filename]:\n                for field in team_fields:\n                    self.registry.register(row.get(field))\n            rows_report[filename] = report\n\n        register_file(\"Brasileirao_Matches.csv\", (\"home_team\", \"away_team\"))\n        register_file(\"Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv\", (\"home_team\", \"away_team\"))\n        register_file(\"Libertadores_Matches.csv\", (\"home_team\", \"away_team\"))\n        register_file(\"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\", (\"home\", \"away\"))\n        register_file(\"novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv\", (\"Equipe_mandante\", \"Equipe_visitante\"))\n        register_file(\"fifa_data.csv\", (\"Club\",))\n        self.registry.finalize()\n\n        builders = [\n            self._build_brasileirao,\n            self._build_cup,\n            self._build_libertadores,\n            self._build_br_football,\n            self._build_novo,\n        ]\n        raw_matches: list[Match] = []\n        for builder in builders:\n            matches, report = builder(parsed)\n            raw_matches.extend(matches)\n            filename = report.pop(\"file\")\n            rows_report.setdefault(filename, {}).update(report)\n        self.raw_matches = raw_matches\n\n        self.matches = self._curate(raw_matches)\n        self._build_indexes()\n        self.players, player_report = self._build_players(parsed[\"fifa_data.csv\"])\n        rows_report[\"fifa_data.csv\"] = player_report\n        self._build_competition_info()\n        self._build_load_report(rows_report)\n\n    # ----------------------------------------------------------- match files\n\n    def _skip_reason(self, row: dict, *, need_date: bool, goals: tuple, teams: tuple, season) -> str | None:\n        for field in teams:\n            if is_nothing(row.get(field)):\n                return f\"missing team ({field})\"\n        if parse_int(season) is None:\n            return \"missing season\"\n        if need_date and parse_date(row.get(goals[0]))[0] is None:\n            return \"missing date\"\n        home_goals, away_goals = parse_int(row.get(goals[1])), parse_int(row.get(goals[2]))\n        if home_goals is None or away_goals is None:\n            return \"missing goals\"\n        return None\n\n    def _make_match(\n        self,\n        *,\n        competition: str,\n        season,\n        match_date,\n        match_time,\n        home_raw,\n        away_raw,\n        home_goals,\n        away_goals,\n        round_no=None,\n        stage=None,\n        stadium=None,\n        source=\"\",\n        stats=None,\n    ) -> Match:\n        return Match(\n            date=match_date,\n            time=match_time,\n            competition=competition,\n            season=int(season),\n            home_team=self.registry.key_for(home_raw),\n            away_team=self.registry.key_for(away_raw),\n            home_display=self.registry.display_for(home_raw),\n            away_display=self.registry.display_for(away_raw),\n            home_goals=int(home_goals),\n            away_goals=int(away_goals),\n            round=parse_int(round_no),\n            stage=stage,\n            stadium=stadium,\n            source=source,\n            **(stats or {}),\n        )\n\n    def _build_brasileirao(self, parsed: dict) -> tuple[list[Match], dict]:\n        report = {\"file\": \"Brasileirao_Matches.csv\", \"rows\": len(parsed[\"Brasileirao_Matches.csv\"]), \"loaded\": 0, \"skipped\": 0}\n        matches: list[Match] = []\n        for row in parsed[\"Brasileirao_Matches.csv\"]:\n            reason = self._skip_reason(\n                row,\n                need_date=True,\n                goals=(\"datetime\", \"home_goal\", \"away_goal\"),\n                teams=(\"home_team\", \"away_team\"),\n                season=row.get(\"season\"),\n            )\n            if reason:\n                report[\"skipped\"] += 1\n                continue\n            match_date, match_time = parse_date(row[\"datetime\"])\n            matches.append(\n                self._make_match(\n                    competition=SERIE_A,\n                    season=row[\"season\"],\n                    match_date=match_date,\n                    match_time=match_time,\n                    home_raw=row[\"home_team\"],\n                    away_raw=row[\"away_team\"],\n                    home_goals=row[\"home_goal\"],\n                    away_goals=row[\"away_goal\"],\n                    round_no=row.get(\"round\"),\n                    source=\"Brasileirao_Matches.csv\",\n                )\n            )\n        report[\"loaded\"] = len(matches)\n        return matches, report\n\n    def _build_cup(self, parsed: dict) -> tuple[list[Match], dict]:\n        report = {\"file\": \"Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv\", \"rows\": len(parsed[\"Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv\"]), \"loaded\": 0, \"skipped\": 0}\n        matches: list[Match] = []\n        for row in parsed[\"Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv\"]:\n            reason = self._skip_reason(\n                row,\n                need_date=True,\n                goals=(\"datetime\", \"home_goal\", \"away_goal\"),\n                teams=(\"home_team\", \"away_team\"),\n                season=row.get(\"season\"),\n            )\n            if reason:\n                report[\"skipped\"] += 1\n                continue\n            match_date, match_time = parse_date(row[\"datetime\"])\n            matches.append(\n                self._make_match(\n                    competition=COPA_DO_BRASIL,\n                    season=row[\"season\"],\n                    match_date=match_date,\n                    match_time=match_time,\n                    home_raw=row[\"home_team\"],\n                    away_raw=row[\"away_team\"],\n                    home_goals=row[\"home_goal\"],\n                    away_goals=row[\"away_goal\"],\n                    round_no=row.get(\"round\"),\n                    source=\"Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv\",\n                )\n            )\n        report[\"loaded\"] = len(matches)\n        return matches, report\n\n    def _build_libertadores(self, parsed: dict) -> tuple[list[Match], dict]:\n        report = {\"file\": \"Libertadores_Matches.csv\", \"rows\": len(parsed[\"Libertadores_Matches.csv\"]), \"loaded\": 0, \"skipped\": 0}\n        matches: list[Match] = []\n        for row in parsed[\"Libertadores_Matches.csv\"]:\n            reason = self._skip_reason(\n                row,\n                need_date=True,\n                goals=(\"datetime\", \"home_goal\", \"away_goal\"),\n                teams=(\"home_team\", \"away_team\"),\n                season=row.get(\"season\"),\n            )\n            if reason:\n                report[\"skipped\"] += 1\n                continue\n            match_date, match_time = parse_date(row[\"datetime\"])\n            stage = clean_text(row.get(\"stage\")) or None\n            matches.append(\n                self._make_match(\n                    competition=LIBERTADORES,\n                    season=row[\"season\"],\n                    match_date=match_date,\n                    match_time=match_time,\n                    home_raw=row[\"home_team\"],\n                    away_raw=row[\"away_team\"],\n                    home_goals=row[\"home_goal\"],\n                    away_goals=row[\"away_goal\"],\n                    stage=stage,\n                    source=\"Libertadores_Matches.csv\",\n                )\n            )\n        report[\"loaded\"] = len(matches)\n        return matches, report\n\n    def _build_br_football(self, parsed: dict) -> tuple[list[Match], dict]:\n        rows = parsed[\"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\"]\n        report = {\"file\": \"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\", \"rows\": len(rows), \"loaded\": 0, \"skipped\": 0}\n        matches: list[Match] = []\n        for row in rows:\n            tournament = row.get(\"tournament\")\n            competition = BR_FOOTBALL_TOURNAMENTS.get(tournament or \"\")\n            if competition is None:\n                report[\"skipped\"] += 1\n                continue\n            reason = self._skip_reason(\n                row,\n                need_date=True,\n                goals=(\"date\", \"home_goal\", \"away_goal\"),\n                teams=(\"home\", \"away\"),\n                season=(row.get(\"date\") or \"\")[:4],\n            )\n            if reason:\n                report[\"skipped\"] += 1\n                continue\n            match_date, _ = parse_date(row[\"date\"])\n            match_time = (row.get(\"time\") or \"\")[:5] or None\n            stats = {\n                \"home_corners\": parse_int(row.get(\"home_corner\")),\n                \"away_corners\": parse_int(row.get(\"away_corner\")),\n                \"home_shots\": parse_int(row.get(\"home_shots\")),\n                \"away_shots\": parse_int(row.get(\"away_shots\")),\n                \"home_attacks\": parse_int(row.get(\"home_attack\")),\n                \"away_attacks\": parse_int(row.get(\"away_attack\")),\n            }\n            matches.append(\n                self._make_match(\n                    competition=competition,\n                    season=(row.get(\"date\") or \"\")[:4],\n                    match_date=match_date,\n                    match_time=match_time,\n                    home_raw=row[\"home\"],\n                    away_raw=row[\"away\"],\n                    home_goals=row[\"home_goal\"],\n                    away_goals=row[\"away_goal\"],\n                    source=\"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\",\n                    stats=stats,\n                )\n            )\n        report[\"loaded\"] = len(matches)\n        return matches, report\n\n    def _build_novo(self, parsed: dict) -> tuple[list[Match], dict]:\n        rows = parsed[\"novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv\"]\n        report = {\"file\": \"novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv\", \"rows\": len(rows), \"loaded\": 0, \"skipped\": 0}\n        matches: list[Match] = []\n        for row in rows:\n            reason = self._skip_reason(\n                row,\n                need_date=True,\n                goals=(\"Data\", \"Gols_mandante\", \"Gols_visitante\"),\n                teams=(\"Equipe_mandante\", \"Equipe_visitante\"),\n                season=row.get(\"Ano\"),\n            )\n            if reason:\n                report[\"skipped\"] += 1\n                continue\n            match_date, _ = parse_date(row[\"Data\"])\n            stadium = (row.get(\"Arena\") or \"\").strip() or None\n            matches.append(\n                self._make_match(\n                    competition=SERIE_A,\n                    season=row[\"Ano\"],\n                    match_date=match_date,\n                    match_time=None,\n                    home_raw=row[\"Equipe_mandante\"],\n                    away_raw=row[\"Equipe_visitante\"],\n                    home_goals=row[\"Gols_mandante\"],\n                    away_goals=row[\"Gols_visitante\"],\n                    round_no=row.get(\"Rodada\"),\n                    stadium=stadium,\n                    source=\"novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv\",\n                )\n            )\n        report[\"loaded\"] = len(matches)\n        return matches, report\n\n    # ---------------------------------------------------------------- players\n\n    _PLAYER_CORE = {\n        \"\", \"ID\", \"Name\", \"Age\", \"Nationality\", \"Overall\", \"Potential\",\n        \"Club\", \"Position\", \"Jersey Number\", \"Height\", \"Weight\",\n        \"Preferred Foot\", \"Value\", \"Wage\",\n    }\n    _PLAYER_MEDIA = {\"Photo\", \"Flag\", \"Club Logo\", \"Real Face\"}\n\n    def _build_players(self, rows: list[dict]) -> tuple[list[Player], dict]:\n        report = {\"rows\": len(rows), \"loaded\": 0, \"skipped\": 0}\n        players: list[Player] = []\n        for row in rows:\n            fifa_id = parse_int(row.get(\"ID\"))\n            name = (row.get(\"Name\") or \"\").strip()\n            if fifa_id is None or not name:\n                report[\"skipped\"] += 1\n                continue\n            club = (row.get(\"Club\") or \"\").strip() or None\n            position = (row.get(\"Position\") or \"\").strip().upper() or None\n            attributes = {\n                key: value\n                for key, value in row.items()\n                if key not in self._PLAYER_CORE\n                and key not in self._PLAYER_MEDIA\n                and value not in (None, \"\")\n            }\n            players.append(\n                Player(\n                    fifa_id=fifa_id,\n                    name=name,\n                    age=parse_int(row.get(\"Age\")),\n                    nationality=(row.get(\"Nationality\") or \"\").strip(),\n                    overall=parse_int(row.get(\"Overall\")),\n                    potential=parse_int(row.get(\"Potential\")),\n                    club=club,\n                    club_key=self.registry.key_for(club) if club else \"\",\n                    position=position,\n                    position_group=position_group(position),\n                    jersey=parse_int(row.get(\"Jersey Number\")),\n                    height=(row.get(\"Height\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n                    weight=(row.get(\"Weight\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n                    preferred_foot=(row.get(\"Preferred Foot\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n                    value=(row.get(\"Value\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n                    wage=(row.get(\"Wage\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n                    attributes=attributes,\n                )\n            )\n        report[\"loaded\"] = len(players)\n        return players, report\n\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------- curation\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _dedup_key(match: Match) -> tuple:\n        return (match.date, match.home_team, match.away_team, match.home_goals, match.away_goals)\n\n    def _curate(self, raw_matches: list[Match]) -> list[Match]:\n        groups: dict[tuple, list[Match]] = defaultdict(list)\n        for match in raw_matches:\n            groups[(match.competition, match.season)].append(match)\n        curated: list[Match] = []\n        merged_stats = 0\n        shadowed = 0\n        for (competition, season), group in groups.items():\n            preference = SOURCE_PREFERENCE[competition]\n            present = {m.source for m in group}\n            chosen = next((src for src in preference if src in present), None)\n            if chosen is None:\n                curated.extend(group)\n                continue\n            kept: dict[tuple, Match] = {}\n            for match in group:\n                if match.source == chosen:\n                    kept.setdefault(self._dedup_key(match), match)\n            for match in group:\n                if match.source == chosen:\n                    continue\n                target = kept.get(self._dedup_key(match))\n                if target is None:\n                    shadowed += 1\n                    continue\n                merged_stats += self._merge(target, match)\n            curated.extend(kept.values())\n        curated.sort(key=lambda m: m.sort_key)\n        self._merge_stats_count = merged_stats\n        self._shadowed_count = shadowed\n        return curated\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _merge(target: Match, donor: Match) -> int:\n        merged = 0\n        for field in (\n            \"stadium\",\n            \"home_corners\", \"away_corners\",\n            \"home_shots\", \"away_shots\",\n            \"home_attacks\", \"away_attacks\",\n        ):\n            if getattr(target, field) is None and getattr(donor, field) is not None:\n                setattr(target, field, getattr(donor, field))\n                merged += 1\n        return merged\n\n    # ---------------------------------------------------------------- indexes\n\n    def _build_indexes(self) -> None:\n        self._by_entity = defaultdict(list)\n        for match in self.matches:\n            self._by_entity[match.home_team].append(match)\n            self._by_entity[match.away_team].append(match)\n        cup_rounds: dict[int, set] = defaultdict(set)\n        for match in self.matches:\n            if match.competition == COPA_DO_BRASIL and match.round is not None:\n                cup_rounds[match.season].add(match.round)\n        self.final_rounds = {season: max(rounds) for season, rounds in cup_rounds.items()}\n\n    def matches_for_entity(self, key: str) -> list[Match]:\n        return self._by_entity.get(key, [])\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------ competition\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def canonical_competition(name: str | None) -> str | None:\n        if not name or is_nothing(name):\n            return None\n        return COMPETITION_ALIASES.get(clean_text(name))\n\n    def list_competitions(self) -> list[str]:\n        return sorted({m.competition for m in self.matches})\n\n    def _build_competition_info(self) -> None:\n        info: dict[str, dict] = {}\n        for match in self.matches:\n            entry = info.setdefault(\n                match.competition,\n                {\"seasons\": {}, \"aliases\": [], \"total_matches\": 0},\n            )\n            entry[\"total_matches\"] += 1\n            season = entry[\"seasons\"].setdefault(\n                match.season,\n                {\"matches\": 0, \"source\": match.source, \"teams\": set()},\n            )\n            season[\"matches\"] += 1\n            season[\"teams\"].add(match.home_team)\n            season[\"teams\"].add(match.away_team)\n        for competition, entry in info.items():\n            entry[\"aliases\"] = sorted(\n                alias for alias, canon in COMPETITION_ALIASES.items() if canon == competition and alias != competition\n            )\n            for season in entry[\"seasons\"].values():\n                season[\"teams\"] = len(season[\"teams\"])\n        self.competition_info = info\n\n    def _build_load_report(self, rows_report: dict) -> None:\n        self.load_report = {\n            \"data_dir\": str(self.data_dir),\n            \"files\": rows_report,\n            \"matches_loaded_raw\": len(self.raw_matches),\n            \"matches_curated\": len(self.matches),\n            \"duplicates_shadowed\": self._shadowed_count,\n            \"stats_fields_merged\": self._merge_stats_count,\n            \"players_loaded\": len(self.players),\n            \"team_entities\": len(self.registry.entities),\n        }\n\n    # ----------------------------------------------------------- lookups\n\n    def resolve_team(self, query: str | None) -> list[TeamEntity]:\n        return self.registry.resolve(query)\n\n    def entity(self, key: str) -> TeamEntity | None:\n        return self.registry.entities.get(key)\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/brazilian_soccer/__init__.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/brazilian_soccer/__init__.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/__init__.py","time":{"start":1788237697734,"end":1788237697743}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now the repository — the biggest module. Let me write it carefully.\n\nKey structures:\n- `TeamRegistry`: raw name → (base, qual); after finalize: raw → entity key; entities dict.\n- `DataRepository`: loads 6 files, builds raw matches, selects sources per (competition, season), merges stats, builds curated list; players.\n\nLoading order for entity registration: I need ALL raw names (match teams + FIFA clubs) before finalize. I'll do:\n1. Read all 6 CSVs into row lists (csv.DictReader).\n2. Register every team/club raw name.\n3. Registry.finalize() → entity ids.\n4. Build Match objects from rows (using registry lookups).\n5. Source selection + merging → curated matches.\n6. Players from fifa rows.\n7. Build competition info + indexes.\n\nFIFA club: raw club names — but note clubs appear with accents \"Grêmio\". Registry gives club_key = entity key. For clubs not appearing elsewhere, entity gets created anyway (e.g. \"fc barcelona\" base). Good.\n\nEntity id rule in finalize:\n- For each raw name → (base, qual). Track base → set of quals (incl None), and (base,qual) → variant counts.\n- For each (base, qual) pair:\n  - non_none_quals = base_quals[base] - {None}\n  - if len(non_none_quals) <= 1 → entity id = base\n  - else → entity id = base + \" \" + qual if qual else base\n  \n  Wait subtle: if base has quals {mg, rn} and pair (america, mg) → id \"america mg\"; pair (america, None) → id \"america\" — a THIRD entity! For \"botafogo\" that's prevented via alias (bare always → rj). Which bases actually have >1 quals AND None variants? Let me handle: if len(non_none) > 1 and qual is None → entity id = base (distinct bare entity). That's the guarani-campinas case IF bare guarani weren't aliased. Fine as a rule.\n\n- TeamEntity.display: most common raw variant; then prettify: if entity id == base (collapsed) → strip trailing qualifier pattern from display (\"Flamengo-RJ\" → \"Flamengo\", \"America MG\" → \"America\"?? hmm — for collapsed entities only, e.g. \"america mg\" is NOT collapsed (qualified) so keeps \"America MG\"). \"Flamengo-RJ\" collapsed → strip \"-RJ\" → \"Flamengo\" ✓. Strip patterns: r\"[-\\s][A-Za-z]{2}$\" only when the 2-letter suffix is a qualifier AND entity collapsed. \"Grêmio\" unchanged ✓. \"Vasco da Gama\" — not collapsed? base \"vasco\"... wait alias made \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" → BASE_ALIASES \"vasco da gama\"→\"vasco\" with qual rj. novo \"Vasco\" bare qual None. quals(\"vasco\") = {rj, None} → collapsed id \"vasco\", display from most common raw... \"Vasco\" or \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" → strip suffix → \"Vasco da Gama\". fine.\n\nSpecial display cleanup: title-case? Keep raw (has accents \"Grêmio\" ✓ prettier).\n\nFor qualified entities: display = most common raw variant (\"America MG\" from BR-Football or \"América-MG\" from novo/Cup/Brasileirao — counts decide). OK.\n\nRegistry.resolve(query):\n```python\ndef resolve(self, query) -> list[TeamEntity]:\n    base, qual = split_team(query)\n    if not base: return []\n    if qual and (key := f\"{base} {qual}\") in self.entities: return [self.entities[key]]\n    if base in self.entities: \n        # exact bare entity OR collapsed entity\n        return [self.entities[base]]\n    # all qualified entities sharing this base\n    same_base = [e for k, e in self.entities.items() if k == base or k.startswith(base + \" \")]\n    if same_base: return same_base\n    # substring fallback\n    subs = [e for k, e in self.entities.items() if base in k]\n    return subs\n```\n\nHmm — careful with the substring fallback matching too broadly (\"atletico\" matches \"atletico alagoinhas\" etc.). Order: exact > same-base > substring. Substring only when no exact/base hits. E.g. query \"barcelona\" → base \"barcelona\" → entities: \"barcelona\" (collapsed, from Barcelona-EQU) + FIFA \"FC Barcelona\" → base \"fc barcelona\"?? cleaned \"fc barcelona\" — hmm BASE alias? \"fc barcelona\" stays base \"fc barcelona\". Substring \"barcelona\" in \"fc barcelona\" ✓ would return both. With exact \"barcelona\" existing (Libertadores), returns just that. OK.\n\nWait — there's an issue with entity registration for FIFA clubs: \"FC Barcelona\" base \"fc barcelona\" — but no qualifier. Unique → id \"fc barcelona\". And query \"barcelona\" exact-matches \"barcelona\" entity only. Fine.\n\nAlso — FIFA \"Juventus\" → \"juventus\"; Brasileirao \"Juventude\" → \"juventude\" ✓ distinct.\n\nNow match loading per file. Source preferences:\n\n```python\nCOMPETITION_SOURCES = {\n    \"Brasileirão Serie A\": [\"Brasileirao_Matches.csv\", \"novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv\", \"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\"],\n    \"Brasileirão Serie B\": [\"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\"],\n    \"Brasileirão Serie C\": [\"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\"],\n    \"Copa do Brasil\": [\"Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv\", \"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\"],\n    \"Copa Libertadores\": [\"Libertadores_Matches.csv\"],\n}\n```\n\nCompetitions canonical names — with accents \"Brasileirão Serie A\". Aliases map (normalized): \"brasileirao serie a\", \"serie a\", \"brasileirao\", \"campeonato brasileiro\" etc.\n\nFor each file parse rows:\n\nBrasileirao_Matches.csv: datetime, home_team, away_team, home_goal, away_goal, season, round, states. → competition \"Brasileirão Serie A\".\n\nnovo: ID, Data, Ano, Rodada, Equipe_mandante, Equipe_visitante, Gols_mandante, Gols_visitante, Vencedor, Arena → competition \"Brasileirão Serie A\", stadium=Arena.\n\nBrazilian_Cup: round (int), datetime, teams, goals, season → \"Copa do Brasil\".\n\nLibertadores: datetime, teams, goals (strings/\"-\"), season (int or NA), stage → \"Copa Libertadores\". Skip rows with missing goals/date/season (the 2022-final NA row).\n\nBR-Football: tournament ∈ {Serie A, Serie B, Serie C, Copa do Brasil} → map to canonical (\"Brasileirão Serie A\" etc.), date, time, goals floats, corners/shots/attacks, ht_diff/at_diff (halftime goals per team? \"ht_diff: 0.0, at_diff: 0.0\" with ht_result DRAW — for [Copa do Brasil, Sao Paulo 1-1 Flamengo] ht_diff=0 at_diff=0 → home 0 - 0 away at half. Second row: Flamengo 0-1 Sao Paulo, ht_diff=-1, at_result WON → home ht goals -1?? That can't be goals. ht_diff = home-away at half? -1 means home trailing by 1 at HT. So ht_diff is a DIFFERENCE not goals. home_ht = (total + diff)/2? No — can't recover individual halves. Hmm: home 0 away 1 final, ht_diff -1 → at HT home trailed by 1 → 0-1. ht_result LOST for home ✓ consistent. For match 1: 1-1, ht_diff 0 → 0-0 or 1-1 at HT — ambiguous! So ht_diff is goal difference at HT; individual HT goals NOT recoverable. I'll store home_ht_diff/away_ht_diff? Not worth it. SKIP halftime entirely — remove those fields from Match. Let me edit models.py to drop home_ht_goals/away_ht_goals... Actually keep them out. I'll edit models later. Or just never set them. Cleaner to remove.\n\nAlso BR-Football time column \"20:00:00\" → time \"20:00\".\n\nfifa: columns as noted. Player attributes: all remaining columns with values.\n\nSkip criteria (load_report counts): missing date, missing/invalid goals, missing teams, missing season.\n\n**Source selection & merge algorithm** (as designed):\n\n```python\ngroups = defaultdict(list)  # (competition, season) -> [Match] in preference order\n```\nTo get preference order: sort raw matches by (competition preference index of source, original order). For each group:\n- chosen_source = first pref source present\n- kept = dedupe([m for m in group if m.source == chosen_source]) by dedup_key\n- donors = others; for each donor: if donor.key in kept_index → fill missing fields (stadium, corners, shots, attacks) → merged++ ; else shadowed++ (dropped)\n- curated.extend(kept)\n\ndedup_key = (date, home_team, away_team, home_goals, away_goals) — entities + score + date. (competition/season already the group.)\n\nHmm — one flaw: within kept (chosen source) two rows with same dedup_key (intra-file dupes, e.g. BR-Football 2021 491 rows — but 2021 not chosen; 2023 chosen with 377 — possible dupes → dedupe handles).\n\nWhat about novo 2012-2019 rows matching Brasileirao keys — donors merge stadium ✓. BR-Football 2014-2022 Serie A donors merge corners ✓.\n\nCup: Brazilian_Cup chosen for 2012-2021; BR-Football 2022/2023 kept as only source ✓. Libertadores: only source ✓.\n\nSerie B/C: BR-Football only ✓.\n\nReport structure:\n```python\nself.load_report = {\n  \"files\": {fname: {\"rows\": n, \"loaded\": n, \"skipped\": n, \"reasons\": {...counters}}},\n  \"matches_raw\": ..., \"matches_curated\": ..., \"merged_stats\": ..., \"shadowed_duplicates\": ...,\n  \"players_loaded\": ...,\n  \"entities\": ...,\n  \"competitions\": {...}\n}\n```\n\n**Competition info**: for canonical comps: seasons dict season → {\"matches\": count, \"source\": file, \"teams\": n}. Plus aliases list.\n\nAlso `list_teams(competition=None)`.\n\n**Indexes** for performance: matches already in-memory; build:\n- self.matches_by_entity: dict entity_key → list[Match]? For team queries. 16k matches × 2 lookups — fine to build once.\n- players sorted by overall desc? Sort at query time (18k players sort ~ms). Fine.\n\nLet me also expose `curated_matches` as `self.matches` and `self.raw_matches` for source-specific search.\n\n`season` type: int. For raw rows with season NA → skipped.\n\nFIFA: club missing (free agents \"No club\"?). Check: some players have Club \"\" or \"Free\"? Handle: club_key \"\" → group \"no club\". is_nothing → club None → display None, club_key \"\". \n\nFIFA nationalities: exact \"Brazil\". Player search by nationality normalized (clean_text equality or accent-insensitive).\n\nNow — the \"finals\" concept for Cup: max round per season. I'll compute in queries: for competition \"Copa do Brasil\", stage filter \"final\" → per-season max round. Let me put a helper in repository: `final_rounds: dict[season, int]` computed from curated cup matches. And Libertadores stage \"final\" exists directly.\n\nLet me now write repository.py. Also handle file-missing gracefully (raise FileNotFoundError with clear message).\n\nOne more decision — **preferred source order within a season when the top source is partial**: not applicable per analysis (Brasileirao complete for all its seasons; novo complete; Cup file complete-ish; BR-Football last resort). Keep simple first-with-data rule.\n\nEdge — what about (competition=\"Copa do Brasil\", season=2012): only Brazilian_Cup ✓. season 2022/2023: BR-Football ✓. \n\nNow writing repository.py.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b44d9b8001KVZgPHkvHm28D7","sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","messageID":"msg_05b438fe4001ZrsMcgjc4sy5jD"}}
