{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788237718342,"sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b44c6ac7e9fc8e47","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"Brazilian soccer MCP server package.\n\nContext: implements the Model Context Protocol server specified in\nTASK.md — a knowledge service over six Kaggle datasets covering\nBrasileirão, Copa do Brasil and Copa Libertadores matches (2003-2023)\nplus a FIFA player database. The package is dependency-free (stdlib\nonly); see server.py for the entry point.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom .models import Match, Player, TeamEntity\nfrom .normalize import clean_text, parse_date, split_team\nfrom .repository import DataRepository\n\n__version__ = \"1.0.0\"\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"DataRepository\",\n    \"Match\",\n    \"Player\",\n    \"TeamEntity\",\n    \"clean_text\",\n    \"parse_date\",\n    \"split_team\",\n    \"__version__\",\n]\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/brazilian_soccer/__init__.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/brazilian_soccer/__init__.py","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/__init__.py","time":{"start":1788237718330,"end":1788237718341}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait — I wrote repository.py content to the wrong path! I wrote it to `brazilian_soccer/__init__.py` instead of `brazilian_soccer/repository.py`. Let me fix: write proper `__init__.py` and move content to `repository.py`. Also I noticed in `_skip_reason`, I use `need_date` param oddly (checking date via goals[0] only when need_date). For BR-Football I passed season as `row[\"date\"][:4]` and goals (\"date\", \"home_goal\", \"away_goal\") — so the date is checked via need_date... wait I passed need_date=True for BR-Football ✓ and for all actually. All five pass need_date=True. Hmm, the parameter is pointless since all use it — but harmless. Actually wait, there's a bug: for BR-Football, `_skip_reason` checks `parse_date(row.get(goals[0]))` where goals[0] = \"date\" ✓ fine.\n\nAnother issue in TeamRegistry.finalize: `self._variant_counts[pair][raw_name] += 0` in register — I add the raw name with count 0 so it's present. Then in finalize, `self._variant_counts[(base, qual)][raw_name] += 1` — adds 1 for each raw name ONCE (registered set). But I want the raw variant COUNT to reflect frequency of appearance! register() only stores each unique name once (dedup via _raw_pairs check) — so counts don't reflect match frequency; display picks \"most common\" but all counts are 1 (first seen). The display heuristic then picks the FIRST raw variant seen. Hmm — that's a problem: \"Flamengo-RJ\" (Brasileirao first) would win over \"Flamengo\" purely by file order. Actually since I strip the suffix for collapsed entities anyway, \"Flamengo-RJ\" → \"Flamengo\" ✓. For qualified entities like \"america mg\": first-seen variant — America-MG (Brasileirao) ✓ fine.\n\nLet me improve: make register() COUNT occurrences (call it for every row occurrence, not just unique). In the file loading, I call register for every row of every file — currently register() early-returns when raw already in _raw_pairs. I'll change to always increment a counter. Let me restructure:\n\n```python\ndef register(self, raw_name):\n    ...\n    self._raw_pairs.setdefault(raw_name, pair)\n    self._variant_counts[pair][raw_name] += 1\n```\nand remove the `+= 1` in finalize (or keep — no, finalize would double-count). Fix this.\n\nAlso in finalize: `entity.qualifiers.add(qual) if qual else entity.qualifiers.add(None)` — statement-as-expression works but ugly; rewrite as if/else. Also qualifiers should collect from all (base,qual) pairs mapping to same entity — for collapsed entities with quals {rj, None} → both merged into one entity: iterating variant_count items gives (base, rj) and (base, None) → same key \"flamengo\" → qualifiers {rj, None} ✓.\n\nBut there's ANOTHER bug in finalize: `self._variant_counts[pair][raw_name] += 0` in register means pair entries exist; then finalize does `for (base, qual), counter in self._variant_counts.items(): self._base_quals[base].add(qual)` ✓. Then `for raw_name, (base, qual) in self._raw_pairs.items(): ... self._variant_counts[(base, qual)][raw_name] += 1` — wait, this increments AGAIN (register already counted). If I change register to count, remove this. Let me rewrite the registry portion.\n\nAlso `_entity_key` uses `self._base_quals` which is filled from `_variant_counts` keys — pairs registered. But `key_for(raw)` uses `self._raw_to_key` built in finalize ✓.\n\nOne more design check — `_entity_key` is called during finalize for both raw_to_key AND entity construction — consistent ✓.\n\nEdge: `key_for` fallback for unregistered names (FIFA club not registered? all registered via register_file(\"fifa_data.csv\", (\"Club\",)) — but clubs with is_nothing skip; those get club_key \"\" ✓).\n\n`display_for` — uses entity display ✓.\n\nAnother bug: in `_build_br_football`, `self._skip_reason(row, need_date=True, goals=(\"date\", ...), season=(row.get(\"date\") or \"\")[:4])` — if date is missing/NA, season \"\" → parse_int None → \"missing season\" reason ✓ but the date check happens first anyway. OK.\n\nBut WAIT — a real bug: `_skip_reason` checks `parse_date(row.get(goals[0]))[0] is None` when need_date — for rows with valid date but season from date[:4] — if date is \"NA\", season \"NA\"[:4]... is_nothing(\"NA\") — parse_int(\"NA\") → None → reason \"missing season\" ✓.\n\nAlso in `_make_match` — `season=int(season)` — season could be str \"2012\" ✓ int() handles.\n\nNow `_build_players` — fifa ID column: \"ID\" ✓. Name \"Name\" ✓. Note row keys include \"\" (index col) — excluded via _PLAYER_CORE containing \"\".\n\n`attributes` excludes media/core; includes skill columns (\"Crossing\", \"LS\"...) ✓.\n\nLet me now rewrite the file properly to repository.py and make __init__.py a proper package init. I'll rewrite the registry section with the counting fix and cleanup.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b461c1f001guqPKhUY7k5tIo","sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","messageID":"msg_05b45d41c001Wc4l23Y5HgLeRk"}}
