{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788237971046,"sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b272870bacc4a5a6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/brazilian_soccer/tools.py","newString":"            _schema({\"name\": _STR, \"id\": _INT}),\n            lambda args: queries.player_detail(repo, player_id=args.pop(\"id\", None), **args),","oldString":"            _schema({\"name\": _STR, \"id\": _INT}),\n            lambda args: queries.player_detail(repo, **args),"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/brazilian_soccer/tools.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/brazilian_soccer/tools.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/brazilian_soccer/tools.py\n@@ -168,9 +168,9 @@\n     \"player_detail\",\n     \"Full FIFA profile (ratings, skills, contract, physical attributes) \"\n     \"for one player by name or FIFA id. Example: 'Gabriel Barbosa'.\",\n     _schema({\"name\": _STR, \"id\": _INT}),\n-    lambda args: queries.player_detail(repo, **args),\n+    lambda args: queries.player_detail(repo, player_id=args.pop(\"id\", None), **args),\n ),\n tool(\n     \"standings\",\n     \"League table calculated from match results for one competition \"\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/brazilian_soccer/tools.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/brazilian_soccer/tools.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/brazilian_soccer/tools.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/brazilian_soccer/tools.py\n@@ -168,9 +168,9 @@\n     \"player_detail\",\n     \"Full FIFA profile (ratings, skills, contract, physical attributes) \"\n     \"for one player by name or FIFA id. Example: 'Gabriel Barbosa'.\",\n     _schema({\"name\": _STR, \"id\": _INT}),\n-    lambda args: queries.player_detail(repo, **args),\n+    lambda args: queries.player_detail(repo, player_id=args.pop(\"id\", None), **args),\n ),\n tool(\n     \"standings\",\n     \"League table calculated from match results for one competition \"\n","additions":1,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/tools.py","time":{"start":1788237971042,"end":1788237971044}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Note: `player_detail` schema declares \"id\" but the query function parameter is `player_id`. Mismatch! The handler does `queries.player_detail(repo, **args)` — args would have \"id\" key → TypeError. Let me align: change query signature to accept `player_id`, and in the handler map: `lambda args: queries.player_detail(repo, player_id=args.pop(\"id\", None), name=args.get(\"name\"))`. Similarly `competition_info` handler: `**args` with \"competition\" ✓.\n\nLet me fix player_detail handler:\n```python\nlambda args: queries.player_detail(repo, player_id=args.pop(\"id\", None), **args),\n```\nBut careful: args may contain \"name\" ✓ passes through.\n\nAlso — argument coercion: MCP clients send JSON per the schema (ints as ints). But be lenient: if season arrives as string \"2019\", query functions use parse_int ✓ handle. limit as string? parse_int ✓.\n\nAnother detail: `call_tool` raising KeyError → protocol layer maps to proper error.\n\nNow protocol.py — MCP over stdio.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b49fb46001LSxWtj2dTh3FN4","sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","messageID":"msg_05b49e637001IbPNKQwqqPF10i"}}
