ndef quick(path):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\n# Where do bare 'atletico'/'bragantino'/'flamengo' come from?\nrows = quick('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv')\nbare = collections.Counter()\nfor r in rows:\n    for side in ('home_team','away_team'):\n        t = r[side].strip()\n        if t.lower() in ('athletico','atletico','flamengo','fluminense','santos','internacional'):\n            bare[t] += 1\nprint(\"Libertadores bare big-club names:\", dict(bare))\n\n# What are the skipped Brasileirao rows?\nrows = quick('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\nskipped = [r for r in rows if r['home_goal'] in ('','NA','-') or r['away_goal'] in ('','NA','-') or r['datetime'] in ('','NA')]\nprint(\"Brasileirao suspicious rows:\", len(skipped))\nfor r in skipped[:5]:\n    print(\"  \", r)\nprint(\"skip seasons:\", collections.Counter(r['season'] for r in skipped))\n\n# Cup skipped\nrows = quick('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv')\ncskipped = [r for r in rows if r['home_goal'] in ('','NA','-') or r['away_goal'] in ('','NA','-') or r['datetime'] in ('','NA')]\nprint(\"Cup suspicious rows:\", len(cskipped), collections.Counter(r['season'] for r in cskipped))\n\n# BR-Football bare names for big clubs in Serie C (flamengo pi?)\nrows = quick('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\nfc = collections.Counter()\nfor r in rows:\n    for side in ('home','away'):\n        t = r[side].strip().lower()\n        if t in ('flamengo','fluminense','santos','internacional','santa cruz','portuguesa','juventude','nautico','bragantino','atletico','river plate','botafogo','gremio','corinthians','palmeiras','sao paulo'):\n            fc[t] += 1\nprint(\"BR-Football bare big-club names:\", dict(fc))\n\n# fifa gabriel barbosa\nrows = quick('data/kaggle/fifa_data.csv')\ngab = [r['Name'] for r in rows if 'gabriel' in r['Name'].lower()]\nprint(\"FIFA Gabriels:\", gab[:20])\nEOF","time":{"start":1788238173260,"end":1788238173276}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Great progress! All champion facts check out:\n- 2003 Cruzeiro ✓, 2012 Fluminense ✓, 2015 Corinthians ✓, 2018 Palmeiras ✓, 2019 Flamengo ✓, 2021 Atlético-MG ✓, 2022 Palmeiras ✓\n- 2019 relegated: Cruzeiro, CSA, Chapecoense, Avaí ✓ (matches real history!)\n\nIssues to address:\n\n1. **2022 champion Palmeiras with 299 matches, not 380** — Brasileirao_Matches.csv has 4180 rows but loaded 4098, skipped 82. Hmm wait — 2022 has only 299 counted matches. Let me check: the file has 380 per season 2012-2022 = 11×380 = 4180. But loaded 4098 — 82 skipped. Why skipped? \"missing team\"? \"missing date\"? \"missing goals\"? Let me investigate — maybe some rows have NA values. 82 skipped... 4180-4098=82. 299 for 2022... so 2022 lost 81 matches! (380-299=81). So 81 of the 82 skipped are 2022 matches. Probably 2022 rows have empty goals or datetime NA (the file may include scheduled-but-unplayed matches at capture time?). Let me check the raw 2022 rows.\n\nAlso \"2022 champion Palmeiras 66 pts from 299 matches\" — that's partial-season. Data completeness note didn't trigger because... expected = 20*19=380, matches 299 < 380 → should show note \"data_complete: false\" — it wasn't printed for 2022 (I only printed relegated/data_complete for 2019). Let me check the skip reasons. If the 2022 rows genuinely lack goals/dates, skipping is correct and the partial-data note is accurate behavior.\n\n2. **Fla-Flu h2h only 22 matches** — way too low! Flamengo vs Fluminense played each other 2x per season × 21 seasons (2003-2022 Serie A) + Cup + Libertadores... should be 50+. PROBLEM. Why so few?\n\nHypothesis: the `flamengo` base is ambiguous now! Look at ambiguous bases: \"flamengo: ['None', 'pi', 'rj']\" — there's a \"Flamengo-PI\" (Flamengo do Piauí, Serie C club!) in BR-Football! So entity \"flamengo\" split into \"flamengo rj\" and \"flamengo pi\" and bare \"flamengo\" entity?? Wait — with >1 quals, my _entity_key gives qualified ids; bare variants map to base \"flamengo\" as separate entity. So \"Flamengo-RJ\" (Brasileirao) → \"flamengo rj\"; \"Flamengo\" (Libertadores/novo/BR-Football) → \"flamengo\" (bare entity, separate!). They got SPLIT into two entities: \"flamengo\" and \"flamengo rj\"!!! That's the bug — exactly what I worried about. Same for fluminense (fluminense-PI exists? \"fluminense: ['None', 'pi', 'rj']\" — Fluminense-PI exists in Serie C data!), santos (\"santos: ['None','ap','sp']\" — Santos-AP!), internacional (Internacional-SC!), sport... etc.\n\nThis is the CRITICAL flaw of the collapse rule: when a small Serie C club shares a base with a giant (Flamengo-PI vs Flamengo-RJ), the giant gets split into TWO entities (bare + rj-qualified). Head-to-head Flamengo vs Fluminense only counted matches where BOTH spellings aligned (both from the same file). 22 matches = probably the subset where both were recorded bare (e.g. BR-Football Serie A?) — inconsistent.\n\nFIX: the FULL_NAME_ALIASES \"bare name → canonical big-club\" approach. For each big club whose base collides with small clubs, alias the BARE form to the big club's qualified key:\n- \"flamengo\" → \"flamengo rj\" (Flamengo do Piauí appears only as \"Flamengo-PI\" qualified, never bare? Let me verify: is there bare \"Flamengo\" in Serie C? BR-Football Serie C would have \"Flamengo PI\"? The qualifier list shows flamengo quals {None, pi, rj} — None comes from bare \"Flamengo\" spellings (Libertadores/novo/BR-Football Serie A \"Flamengo\"). Is bare \"Flamengo\" ever used for the PI club? Unlikely — the PI club is always \"Flamengo-PI\" or \"Flamengo PI\" (qualified, since disambiguation needed within Serie C). Hmm — but BR-Football has \"Flamengo\" bare in Serie A rows AND possibly \"Flamengo PI\" in Serie C rows. So aliasing bare \"flamengo\" → \"flamengo rj\" is CORRECT (bare always = the big club).\n- \"fluminense\" → \"fluminense rj\" (Fluminense-PI exists similarly; Fluminense de Feira is a distinct base ✓)\n- \"santos\" → \"santos sp\" (Santos-AP = Santos Futebol Clube do Amapá; bare \"Santos\" = Pelé's club ✓)\n- \"internacional\" → \"internacional rs\" (Internacional-SC exists; bare = Colorado ✓)\n- \"santa cruz\" → \"santa cruz pe\" — quals {pe, rn, rs}: Santa Cruz-RN, Santa Cruz-RS small clubs. bare = Recife ✓\n- \"portuguesa\" → \"portuguesa sp\" (Portuguesa-RJ exists) ✓\n- \"juventude\" → \"juventude rs\" (Juventude-MA exists) ✓\n- \"nautico\" → \"nautico pe\" (Náutico-RR exists) ✓\n- \"bragantino\"? — \"bragantino: ['None','pa','sp']\" — Bragantino-PA (small) vs Red Bull Bragantino-SP... wait \"bragantino\" base with quals pa/sp — Bragantino-PA is \"Bragantino Clube do Pará\"? And Red Bull Bragantino is a DIFFERENT base \"red bull bragantino\" ✓. Is there bare \"Bragantino\"? quals include None — hmm, \"Bragantino\" bare... In novo? Bragantino-SP (old name of RB Bragantino, 2019-2021 Serie A as \"Red Bull Bragantino\"; in 2018 Serie B it was \"Bragantino-SP\"?). BR-Football might have \"Bragantino\" bare = SP club. Alias \"bragantino\" → \"bragantino sp\"? Careful: Bragantino-PA is Serie D/C club, always qualified. Bare = SP club (historical). Add alias ✓.\n- \"atletico\" bare — quals {None, ac, ba, es, go, mg, pr}: WAIT — \"atletico\" has None?! Which file has BARE \"Atlético\"/\"Atletico\"?? Hmm — Libertadores! \"Athletico\" bare?? The Libertadores NA row was \"Flamengo vs Athletico\" (final) — skipped (no goals). But maybe other Libertadores rows have bare \"Athletico\"? Yes! Libertadores file probably spells Brazilian clubs WITHOUT suffixes sometimes (\"Flamengo\", \"Athletico\"?). Earlier sample showed \"Atlético-MG\" with suffix in finals. Hmm, \"atletico\" bare with None... Could be from \"Athletico\" bare in Libertadores 2022 (Athletico-PR ran to final 2022 — the NA row \"Flamengo vs Athletico\" is that final!). Other Libertadores matches may use \"Athletico\" bare. So bare \"atletico\" = Athletico-PR (Paraná) in Libertadores context! But aliasing bare \"atletico\" → \"atletico pr\" — hmm, is that right? In ALL files, bare \"Atletico\" (if any)... FIFA? FIFA has \"Atlético Madrid\", \"Atlético Mineiro\", \"Atlético Paranaense\" — all full names, no bare \"Atlético\". BR-Football: \"Atletico Alagoinhas\" etc. — no bare \"Atletico\". So bare \"atletico\" comes only from Libertadores \"Athletico\" (2022 semifinals/final rows?). Let me verify where bare atletico appears. If it's Libertadores \"Athletico\" → it's the PR club → alias \"atletico\" → \"atletico pr\"?? Hmm — but that would be WRONG if... let me check the raw data first.\n\n  Wait, also \"atletico\" quals include ac, ba, es: \"Atlético-AC\"? (Atlético Acreano — base \"atletico acreano\"? no — \"Atletico Acreano\" base is \"atletico acreano\"... hmm where does ac come from? Maybe \"Atlético-AC\" spelled in some file. ba = \"Atlético de Alagoinhas\"→ \"atletico alagoinhas\"? no. \"Atlético-BA\"? Maybe BR-Football \"Atletico Baiano\"? Hmm. es = \"Atlético-ES\"? Whatever — small clubs, always qualified.\n\n- \"river plate\" {None, se, uru}: bare \"River Plate\"?? — hmm, where? Libertadores has \"River Plate-URU\" (qualified). Bare \"River Plate\" — Libertadores file might have Argentine \"River Plate\" bare! quals se = \"River Plate-SE\" (Sergipe club!). So bare \"river plate\" = the ARGENTINE club (big). Alias \"river plate\" → ... the Argentine club has no qualifier. Hmm — entity keys: \"river plate se\" (small), \"river plate uru\" (Uruguayan), and bare \"river plate\" entity = Argentine. With alias approach I'd map bare → which? There's no canonical qualifier for the Argentine club. It stays as its own entity \"river plate\" (bare) — actually that's FINE here: Argentine River only appears bare, Uruguayan only as -URU, Sergipe as -SE. No split problem for the big club since it never appears qualified! The PROBLEM only occurs when a big club appears BOTH bare AND qualified. That's exactly the flamengo/fluminense/santos/internacional/santa cruz/portuguesa/juventude/nautico case (RJ/SP/RS/PE big clubs appear bare in some files and -UF in others).\n\nSo the fix: add FULL_NAME_ALIASES for bare→qualified for the clubs that appear both ways:\n- \"flamengo\" → \"flamengo rj\"\n- \"fluminense\" → \"fluminense rj\"\n- \"santos\" → \"santos sp\"\n- \"internacional\" → \"internacional rs\"\n- \"santa cruz\" → \"santa cruz pe\"\n- \"portuguesa\" → \"portuguesa sp\"\n- \"juventude\" → \"juventude rs\"\n- \"nautico\" → \"nautico pe\"\n- \"bragantino\" → \"bragantino sp\" — hmm wait, \"bragantino\" bare... let me check whether bare bragantino exists and from where. Might be from... let me check.\n\nAnd verify no OTHER big club has both bare+qualified split. From the \"BASES WITH None + qualifier(s)\" list, the ones with None AND ≥1 quals where the None belongs to the BIG club:\n- flamengo {None, pi, rj} → FIX alias → rj\n- fluminense {None, pi, rj} → FIX → rj\n- santos {None, ap, sp} → FIX → sp\n- internacional {None, rs, sc} → FIX → rs\n- santa cruz {None, pe, rn, rs} → FIX → pe\n- portuguesa {None, rj, sp} → FIX → sp (Portuguesa-RJ small, Lusa big bare)\n- juventude {None, ma, rs} → FIX → rs\n- nautico {None, pe, rr} → FIX → pe\n- sport {None, pe} → single non-None qual → collapses fine already ✓\n- bragantino {None, pa, sp} → bare = ? check\n- atletico {None, ac, ba, es, go, mg, pr} → bare = ? check (probably Libertadores \"Athletico\")\n- river plate {None, se, uru} → bare stays as Argentine club ✓ acceptable (never qualified)\n- ypiranga {None, ap, rs} — two small clubs, bare from? eh — Ypiranga-AP vs Ypiranga-RS, both Serie C/D — bare \"Ypiranga\" appears where? maybe BR-Football \"Ypiranga\" bare (RS? or AP?). Small clubs, low stakes. Leave.\n\nEverything else in the None+quals list has exactly ONE qualifier (auto-collapse ✓ e.g. \"ceara {None, ce}\" → \"ceara\").\n\nSo: which spellings produce bare \"atletico\"/\"bragantino\"? Let me check the raw data. Also double-check \"flamengo\" bare sources.\n\n3. **Gabriel Barbosa not found** — the FIFA dataset's name is probably \"Gabriel Barbosa\"?? Sample showed names like 'Neymar Jr', 'Casemiro'... Gabigol in FIFA 19 is \"Gabriel Barbosa\" at Inter Milan. Hmm — search was substring on clean name. Let me check what names exist: grep fifa for \"Gabriel\". Maybe \"G. Barbosa\"? Let me check.\n\n4. **2022 partial data** — check why 82 rows skipped (probably unplayed fixtures with empty goals). The standings note should then mark 2022 partial — expected 380, got 299 → data_complete False + note ✓ good behavior. Also Flamengo 2022 relegated check: 2019 relegated list shows \"Avai\" (display \"Avai\" — hmm display for avaí... fine) and \"Csa\" — displays look off (\"Csa\" vs \"CSA\") but entity keys are right. Display for CSA: variants \"Csa-AL\" (Brasileirao, stripped → \"Csa\")? display picked most common raw \"Csa\" from \"Csa-AL\"? Wait Brasileirao has \"Csa-AL\" → display strip suffix → \"Csa\". Ideally \"CSA\". Cosmetic — acceptable. Actually let me improve display: strip-suffix produces \"Csa\"; the raw was \"Csa-AL\" (already unaccented weird). Leave it.\n\nHmm wait — actually there's a subtlety with display stripping for collapsed entities: \"Cruzeiro\" display ✓. \"Fluminense-RJ\" — champion 2012 display \"Fluminense-RJ\"! That entity is \"fluminense rj\"?? No wait — 2012 champion display showed \"Fluminense-RJ\" — but after my fix (alias bare→rj) entity \"fluminense rj\" display would be \"Fluminense-RJ\" (most common variant with suffix)... Display for big clubs will be e.g. \"Flamengo-RJ\". Hmm — the 2019 champion showed \"Flamengo-RJ\" (before fix, entity \"flamengo rj\" existed from qualified spellings only... it showed Flamengo-RJ with 90 pts — those were the Brasileirao-file matches only!). After the alias fix, entity \"flamengo rj\" will include bare spellings too; display = most common raw = \"Flamengo-RJ\" (Brasileirao file has ~2×380? more rows than bare...). Hmm — \"Flamengo-RJ\" as display is OK but \"Flamengo\" nicer. For QUAL