pped 16 — same reason probably (unplayed/NA). Fine.\n\n6. **Fla-Flu after fix** should be ~40+ matches (2 per season × 17 Serie A seasons 2003-2019 from novo/Brasileirao + 2020-2022 + cup meetings).\n\n7. **stats_summary Serie A**: 8321 matches, avg 2.57 goals — plausible (spec example said 2.47 but that's their example, ours is data-real).\n\n8. **Biggest wins**: 2021-06-08 \"Sao Paulo 9-1 4 de Julho (Copa do Brasil 2021)\" — wait, Sao Paulo 9-1 4 de Julho? Hmm, that's from Brazilian_Cup_Matches 2021? Actually 2021 Copa do Brasil... São Paulo beat 4 de Julho? Hmm, no — I recall São Paulo 9-1 4 de Julho?? Hmm... there might be a data quirk: that match is from Cup file 2021 (round 1). Hmm wait actually I recall Botinudo... whatever — it's in the data. Hmm, hold on: \"4 de Julho\" beat... no wait. Actually I DO recall: Copa do Brasil 2021 first round: 4 de Julho-PB... no. Let me not question; it's what the dataset says. Actually hmm — São Paulo played Copa do Brasil 2021?? São Paulo entered... yes all big clubs enter Copa do Brasil. São Paulo vs 4 de Julho? Hmm... maybe. Fine — data is data; the tool reports it.\n\nHmm wait, one thing to verify: 2021 Cup source selection — Brazilian_Cup_Matches has 2021 rounds 1-4 only (data showed rounds [1,2,3,4] for 2021). So Cup 2021 in curated = rounds 1-4 (partial season, file limitation) ✓ acceptable.\n\n9. **Palmeiras 2023 cross-file** — output below got cut (crashed before). Re-run after fixes.\n\n10. **stadium/corners merge** — crashed before printing. Re-check after fix.\n\n11. **\"Flamengo\" resolve** — after alias: resolve(\"Flamengo\") → base \"flamengo\", qual None → alias → (\"flamengo\",\"rj\") → qual path: \"flamengo rj\" in entities → [entity] ✓ single! And resolve(\"Flamengo-RJ\") → same ✓. \n\n12. **display for collapsed small clubs**: fine.\n\nAlso — skip reason counting: let me record skip reasons in the report for transparency. Let me add a Counter of reasons per file. Quick change in _skip_reason usage... I'll