9). So:\n   - \"flamengo\" bare → RJ club ✓ alias\n   - \"fluminense\" bare → RJ ✓\n   - \"santos\" bare → SP ✓\n   - \"internacional\" bare → RS ✓\n   - \"juventude\" bare → RS ✓ (BR-Football Serie B)\n   - \"bragantino\" bare (358!) → Red Bull Bragantino? OR old Bragantino-SP... In BR-Football 2014-2023, \"Bragantino\" bare = Bragantino-SP (later Red Bull). Hmm — base \"bragantino\" quals {None, pa, sp}: where does \"bragantino pa\" come from? \"Bragantino-PA\" (Série D club). The bare \"bragantino\" 358 rows = the SP club. BUT — there's ALSO base \"red bull bragantino\" {None, sp}! So \"Red Bull Bragantino-SP\" (2019+ Brasileirao) and bare \"Bragantino\" (BR-Football) are the same club in different eras! Hmm. Should I alias \"bragantino\" → \"red bull bragantino\"? The club was renamed in 2019. For head-to-head continuity, yes they're the same club (Bragantino = RB Bragantino). I'll add alias \"bragantino sp\"→? hmm.\n   \n   Actually cleaner: alias bare \"bragantino\" → \"red bull bragantino\"?? But \"Bragantino-SP\" qualified (from where? maybe BR-Football \"Bragantino SP\"? or novo?) → base \"bragantino\" qual \"sp\" → that should ALSO map to red bull bragantino... So BASE-level: any (bragantino, sp) or (bragantino, None) → \"red bull bragantino\". I can add to FULL_NAME_ALIASES: \"bragantino\" → \"red bull bragantino\" and \"bragantino sp\" → \"red bull bragantino\". FULL aliases match the full cleaned string: \"bragantino\" bare → alias ✓; \"bragantino sp\" → alias ✓; \"bragantino pa\" → stays ✓. \n   \n   Hmm wait, but do I WANT Bragantino-2014 merged with RB Bragantino-2019? They're the same legal club (rebrand). Yes, merge is correct for h2h purposes. \n\n   And \"atletico\" bare (Libertadores \"Athletico\" = Athletico-PR 2022) → alias \"atletico\"→? bare \"atletico\" → \"atletico pr\"?? — but hold on: is bare \"Atletico\" EVER used for another club in any file? BR-Football bare \"atletico\"? The counter didn't include 'atletico' → 0 bare atletico in BR-Football. Libertadores \"Athletico\" bare = PR ✓. So alias \"athletico\" → \"atletico pr\" and \"atletico\" → \"atletico pr\"?? Hmm — dangerous: \"atletico\" bare could be... only Libertadores Athletico. But wait — what about BASE_ALIASES \"athletico\"→\"atletico\": Libertadores bare \"Athletico\" → cleaned \"athletico\" → BASE alias → base \"atletico\" qual None → entity \"atletico\" (bare entity since >1 quals) — SPLIT from \"atletico pr\"! So I need FULL alias \"athletico\" → \"atletico pr\" and... \"atletico\" bare → \"atletico pr\" too? If I alias bare \"atletico\" → \"atletico pr\", then any FUTURE bare \"atletico\" meaning MG would break — but in THIS data, bare atletico only appears as Libertadores Athletico (PR) ✓. Add both aliases: \"athletico\" → \"atletico pr\", \"atletico\" → \"atletico pr\".\n\n   Hmm wait — actually careful with \"Athletico\" bare in Libertadores: 2022 Libertadores has Athletico-PR as \"Athletico\"? The NA final row was \"Flamengo vs Athletico\". And 29 bare Athletico rows — the 2022 run (group 6 + knockouts). So yes PR club. ✓\n\n   - \"river plate\" bare — from where? quals {None, se, uru}. Libertadores \"River Plate\" (Argentine) bare? Hmm — earlier counter didn't check 'river plate'. It's fine — Argentine River as bare entity \"river plate\", Uruguayan \"river plate uru\", Sergipe \"river plate se\" — no big-club split issue. Leave.\n   - \"santa cruz\" bare {None, pe, rn, rs} — bare from novo (\"Santa Cruz\" = Recife PE ✓) → alias \"santa cruz\" → \"santa cruz pe\".\n   - \"portuguesa\" bare {None, rj, sp} — bare from novo/BR-Football (\"Portuguesa\" = SP ✓) → alias → \"portuguesa sp\".\n   - \"nautico\" bare → \"nautico pe\" ✓ (novo \"Náutico\").\n   - \"botafogo\" already aliased ✓. \"gremio\"/\"corinthians\"/\"palmeiras\"/\"sao paulo\" — quals {None, sp/mg/rs} single qual → auto-collapse ✓ no fix needed.\n   - \"vitoria\" already aliased ✓.\n   - \"ypiranga\" small clubs, skip.\n   - \"nacional\" {am, par, uru} — no bare ✓ fine ( Nacional-AM small BR club, Nacional PAR/URU). ✓ distinct.\n   - \"guarani\" aliased ✓.\n\n3. **Gabriel Barbosa NOT in FIFA data** — the Gabriels list has no \"Gabriel Barbosa\". FIFA 19 must name him differently... he's not there at all (maybe he's \"G. Barbosa\"? not in list either). So the spec's example \"Who is Gabriel Barbosa?\" can't be answered from this dataset — data limitation, tool correctly raises QueryError. For tests I'll use players that exist (Neymar Jr, Alisson, Gabriel Jesus ✓ he's there!). The player_detail error message is the correct behavior. Also the spec example listing \"Neymar Jr - Overall: 92\" ✓ matches (we got Neymar 92 ✓!).\n\nSo the fixes needed in normalize.py FULL_NAME_ALIASES:\n```python\n\"flamengo\": \"flamengo rj\",\n\"fluminense\": \"fluminense rj\",\n\"santos\": \"santos sp\",\n\"internacional\": \"internacional rs\",\n\"juventude\": \"juventude rs\",\n\"nautico\": \"nautico pe\",\n\"santa cruz\": \"santa cruz pe\",\n\"portuguesa\": \"portuguesa sp\",\n\"bragantino\": \"red bull bragantino\",\n\"bragantino sp\": \"red bull bragantino\",\n\"athletico\": \"atletico pr\",\n\"atletico\": \"atletico pr\",\n```\n\nHmm — wait, \"atletico\" → \"atletico pr\": but then _split_qualifier on \"atletico pr\" gives base \"atletico\" qual \"pr\" ✓. But careful: alias lookup happens BEFORE split: cleaned \"atletico\" → alias → \"atletico pr\" → split ✓.\n\nBut hold on — what about \"Atletico-MG\" cleaned \"atletico mg\"? → not an alias key ✓ → split → (\"atletico\", \"mg\") ✓. Good.\n\nAnd what about the Brasileirao \"Atletico-PR\" (qualified) → \"atletico pr\" ✓ same as aliased bare. ✓\n\nNow — RED BULL BRAGANTINO: \"Red Bull Bragantino-SP\" → cleaned \"red bull bragantino sp\" → split → base \"red bull bragantino\" qual \"sp\" → quals {sp, None}? Is there bare \"Red Bull Bragantino\"? Maybe in BR-Football \"Red Bull Bragantino\" (no state) ✓ → single qual sp → collapse → entity \"red bull bragantino\" ✓. Alias \"bragantino\" → \"red bull bragantino\" → split → base \"red bull bragantino\" qual None → hmm! The alias target has NO qualifier — bare \"bragantino\" (BR-Football) maps to (\"red bull bragantino\", None) → entity \"red bull bragantino\" ✓ (collapsed with sp) ✓✓. And \"bragantino sp\" qualified → alias → \"red bull bragantino\" → qual None ✓ same entity ✓. \n\nAlso \"Bragantino-PA\" → \"bragantino pa\" not aliased → (\"bragantino\", \"pa\") → quals(\"bragantino\") = {pa} — wait, after aliasing away all bare/sp forms, base \"bragantino\" only has qual \"pa\" → single → collapse → entity \"bragantino\" (the PA club) ✓ distinct from \"red bull bragantino\" ✓ \n\nNow also — the \"atletico\" entity: after aliasing bare away, base \"atletico\" quals = {ac, ba, es, go, mg, pr} (no None) → qualified entities \"atletico mg\", \"atletico pr\", etc. ✓ and the Brasileirao \"Atletico-GO\"/\"Atletico-MG\"/\"Atletico-PR\", Libertadores \"Athletico\"(aliased to pr) ✓ all consistent. \n\nOne more — \"delfin {None, equ}\" — Libertadores \"Delfín-EQU\" → (\"delfin\", \"equ\")... wait quals shows None AND equ. \"Delfin\" bare appears somewhere (BR-Football \"Delfin\"? no — maybe Libertadores \"Delfín\" bare somewhere). Single non-None qual → collapse → \"delfin\" ✓ fine.\n\n\"libertad {None, par}\" ✓ collapse fine. \"penarol {None, am}\" — Penarol-AM?? \"Peñarol\" (Uruguay) bare + \"Penarol-AM\" (Brazilian Amazonas club?!) — collapse would MERGE Uruguayan Peñarol with Penarol-AM!! quals {None, am} → single non-None (am) → collapse → ONE entity \"penarol\" merging both! Hmm — do they coexist in same competitions? Penarol-AM in Serie C, Peñarol in Libertadores. Merging them is WRONG but... how often? Let me check \"Penarol-AM\" in BR-Football. If it exists, I should alias bare \"penarol\" → \"penarol uru\"? or keep them split by making Penarol-AM qualified... The collapse rule merges when exactly ONE non-None qual. To split, alias: \"penarol\" → \"penarol uru\" (bare always = Uruguayan big club in Libertadores). Let me check the data... Actually \"penarol {None, am}\" — where's the am from? BR-Football Serie C 2014-2023 could have \"Penarol AM\". Let me check and add alias if needed. Similarly check other None+single-qual bases where None is a DIFFERENT club from the qualified one. This is the \"small club with same name as foreign big club\" pattern: penarol (URU vs AM). Others? \"river plate\" handled. \"nacional\" {am, par, uru} — no None ✓. \"olimpia\"? probably {par} only. \"barcelona\" {equ} only. Let me check \"penarol\" quickly and add the alias if needed.\n\nAlso — I realize there may be an issue with **\"America\" Cup spelling**: \"América - MG\" cleaned → \"america mg\" ✓ handled.\n\nLet me also double check **\"Sao Paulo\" bare (BR-Football 426)** → base \"sao paulo\" qual None; \"Sao Paulo-SP\" (Brasileirao) qual sp → quals {None, sp} single → collapse \"sao paulo\" ✓ fine.\n\nAnd **\"gremio\" bare** {None, rs} → collapse ✓. **\"corinthians\"** ✓. **\"palmeiras\"** ✓. **\"cruzeiro\"** ✓. **\"bahia\"** ✓ etc.\n\nNow implement:\n1. normalize.py: add aliases.\n2. Re-run dev_check → verify Fla-Flu count jumps to ~40+, Palmeiras 2023, stadium/corners merges, derby counts.\n\nThen also fix: the dev_check \"BASES WITH None\" listing will shrink.\n\nAlso add \"reasons\" to skip report? Nice-to-have; let me add a reasons counter to the load report for the skipped rows — helps users understand 2022 is partial. Quick: in each builder, count reasons. I'll add it — small change, better transparency. Actually — keep the report as is but ADD \"reasons\" dict. Let me do it minimally: modify _skip_reason to return reason string (already does) and builders increment report[\"skipped\"] — add `report.setdefault(\"skip_reasons\", Counter())[reason] += 1`. Hmm, Counter import in repository — already imported. Let me add to all 5 builders. Simpler: wrap in a helper... it's fine, small edits.\n\nLet me apply the normalize.py alias fixes first.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"