alse},"title":"brazilian_soccer/normalize.py","time":{"start":1788238418685,"end":1788238418688}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"So \"Bragantino PA\" — that's Clube Atlético Bragantino? No wait — \"Bragantino-PA\" is the Pará club (Bragantino FC do Pará?). Hmm — but wait, hold on: \"Bragantino PA\" 4 matches in Serie C/D context. And \"Bragantino\" bare 358 = the SP club (in Serie B 2014-2019 as Bragantino, then... wait — BR-Football Serie B 2014-2023: the club appears as \"Bragantino\" even after rebrand? and \"Red Bull Bragantino\" appears in Brasileirao file as \"Red Bull Bragantino-SP\" ✓ merged via alias to \"red bull bragantino\".\n\nHmm — but \"Bragantino PA\"... hmm, actually — hmm. There's a real club \"Bragantino Clube do Pará\" (from Bragança, Pará). Yes. So my handling: \"Bragantino PA\" → base \"bragantino\" qual \"pa\" → entity \"bragantino\" (collapsed, since base bragantino now only has qual pa... wait the ambiguous list shows \"red bull bragantino: ['None','pa','sp']\" — meaning base \"red bull bragantino\" got quals None, pa, sp! So \"Bragantino PA\" must have mapped to \"red bull bragantino pa\"?! How?\n\nOH NO — I see the bug! My alias is applied to the FULL CLEANED STRING in split_team:\n```\ncleaned = FULL_NAME_ALIASES.get(cleaned, cleaned)\n```\n\"Bragantino PA\" → cleaned \"bragantino pa\" — not an alias key ✓ → split → base \"bragantino\", qual \"pa\". Then:\n```\nbase = BASE_ALIASES.get(base, base)  # no\nif base != cleaned and base in FULL_NAME_ALIASES:  # \"bragantino\" != \"bragantino pa\" AND \"bragantino\" IS an alias key!\n    expanded = FULL_NAME_ALIASES[base]  # \"red bull bragantino\"\n    base, extra = _split_qualifier(expanded)  # (\"red bull bragantino\", None)\n    base = BASE_ALIASES.get(base, base)\n    qualifier = qualifier or extra  # \"pa\"\n```\nSo (\"bragantino\", \"pa\") → (\"red bull bragantino\", \"pa\")!! WRONG — the Pará club got folded into \"red bull bragantino pa\"!\n\nThat re-expansion block is too aggressive: it re-applies FULL aliases to the DE-QUALIFIED base for ANY base that happens to be an alias key — including when the original string had a DIFFERENT qualifier. The purpose of that block was for cases like \"Vitória-BA\" (base \"vitoria\" → alias \"vitoria ba\" to pin the qualifier) — where the alias CONFIRMS the same qualifier. The bug: when qualifier differs from the alias target's, we get nonsense.\n\nFix: in the re-expansion block, only use the expansion if `extra == qualifier` (alias confirms) or `qualifier is None`... wait no — the block runs when qualifier is NOT None (base came from a qualified spelling). Cases:\n- \"Vitória-BA\" → (vitoria, ba): expansion \"vitoria ba\" → extra \"ba\" == qual \"ba\" ✓ keep base \"vitoria\" qual \"ba\" (no change effectively).\n- \"Botafogo-PB\" → (botafogo, pb): expansion \"botafogo rj\" → extra \"rj\" ≠ \"pb\" → DON'T expand (keep botafogo pb) ✓ desired!\n- \"Guarani-PAR\" → (guarani, par): expansion \"guarani sp\" → extra \"sp\" ≠ \"par\" → don't expand ✓ desired (guarani par stays Paraguayan).\n- \"Flamengo-PI\" → (flamengo, pi): expansion \"flamengo rj\" → extra \"rj\" ≠ \"pi\" → don't expand ✓ desired.\n- \"Bragantino-PA\" → (bragantino, pa): expansion \"red bull bragantino\" → extra None ≠ \"pa\" → don't expand ✓ desired.\n- \"Santos-AP\" → (santos, ap): expansion \"santos sp\" extra sp ≠ ap → don't expand ✓.\n\nSo rule: re-expand ONLY when `extra == qualifier`. When does the re-expansion matter at all then? For \"Vitória-BA\": base \"vitoria\" + qual \"ba\"; expansion \"vitoria ba\" → (\"vitoria\", \"ba\") — identical, no-op. Hmm — so with the `extra == qualifier` restriction, the block is nearly a no-op... EXCEPT when expansion changes the BASE: e.g. alias \"bragantino\" → \"red bull bragantino\" — for spelling \"Bragantino-SP\" → (bragantino, sp): expansion \"red bull bragantino\" → extra None ≠ sp → NO expansion → \"bragantino sp\" stays separate from \"red bull bragantino\"!! But I aliased \"bragantino sp\" → \"red bull bragantino\" in FULL_NAME_ALIASES (full-string match) so \"Bragantino-SP\" cleaned \"bragantino sp\" hits the FIRST alias lookup ✓. OK.\n\nWhat about \"Corinthians-SP\" → (corinthians, sp): \"corinthians\" is NOT an alias key → no expansion ✓.\n\nHmm — when IS the re-expansion block needed with extra==qualifier? \"Vitória-BA\" no-op... Let me think about \"Atletico-PR\" → (atletico, pr): \"atletico\" IS an alias key → expansion \"atletico pr\" → extra \"pr\" == qual \"pr\" ✓ expand → (atletico, pr) — no-op again. \n\nSo actually — with the restriction, the block only ever confirms what we already have... EXCEPT aliases whose target changes the base with same qualifier: e.g. hypothetical \"bragantino sp\" (base bragantino, qual sp) — expansion \"red bull bragantino\" extra None ≠ sp → blocked. But that spelling hits the full-string alias anyway.\n\nSo the simplest correct fix: DELETE the re-expansion block entirely. Let me trace all cases without it:\n- \"Botafogo-PB\" → (botafogo, pb) ✓\n- \"Vitória-BA\" → cleaned \"vitoria ba\" — FIRST alias lookup: \"vitoria ba\" not a key → split → (vitoria, ba) ✓ (I have alias \"vitoria\"→\"vitoria ba\" for BARE only ✓)\n- \"Guarani-PAR\" → (guarani, par) ✓\n- \"Flamengo-PI\" → (flamengo, pi) ✓ — wait, does the FIRST lookup catch \"flamengo pi\"? No (\"flamengo pi\" not a key) → split → base \"flamengo\" qual \"pi\" ✓ \n- \"Atletico-MG\" → \"atletico mg\" not a key → (atletico, mg) ✓ \n- bare \"Atletico\" → first lookup \"atletico\" IS a key → \"atletico pr\" → split → (atletico, pr) ✓\n- \"Bragantino PA\" → \"bragantino pa\" not a key → (bragantino, pa) ✓ entity \"bragantino\" (PA club, collapsed since only qual) ✓ SEPARATE from red bull bragantino ✓✓\n- \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" → \"vasco da gama rj\" not a key → split → base \"vasco da gama\" qual rj → BASE_ALIASES → \"vasco\" ✓ (BASE_ALIASES still applied after split ✓)\n- \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" → paren → \"america fc mg\" → not a key?? hmm wait — FULL alias has \"america fc\" → \"america mg\" but the cleaned string is \"america fc mg\" (paren turned into qual mg). Not a key → split → base \"america fc\" qual \"mg\" → BASE_ALIASES \"america fc\"→\"america\" → (\"america\", \"mg\") ✓ \n\nAll correct WITHOUT the re-expansion block. And the block was actively harmful (Bragantino-PA bug). DELETE it.\n\nAlso — hmm, one more case to verify after deletion: FIFA \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" — paren check: \"minas gerais\" in PAREN_STATE_NAMES → \" mg\" ✓ → \"america fc mg\" ✓ → (\"america\",\"mg\") ✓ joins America-MG ✓.\n\nNow — \"Bragantino\" bare (358 rows, BR-Football Serie B) → alias → \"red bull bragantino\" → (red bull bragantino, None) → entity \"red bull bragantino\" ✓. And \"Red Bull Bragantino-SP\" → (red bull bragantino, sp) ✓ same entity (single qual sp → collapse... wait quals for base \"red bull bragantino\" = {None, sp} → single non-None → collapse → entity \"red bull bragantino\" ✓ MERGED ✓.\n\nAnd \"Bragantino PA\" → entity \"bragantino\" (PA club) ✓ separate ✓.\n\nLet me remove the re-expansion block from split_team.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b50c0d400169fzvL9eVeYc6u","sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","messageID":"msg_05b5020d8001f4w82j0Zsxtu40"}}
