{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788238658699,"sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8410363856e01369","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0, \".\")\nfrom brazilian_soccer.repository import DataRepository\nfrom brazilian_soccer import queries\nrepo = DataRepository()\n\n# Corinthians home 2019 (complete season)\nts = queries.team_stats(repo, \"Corinthians\", season=2019)\nprint(\"Corinthians 2019:\", ts[\"overall\"], \"| home:\", ts[\"home\"])\n\n# Libertadores 2019 final\nf = queries.search_matches(repo, competition=\"Libertadores\", season=2019, stage=\"final\")\nfor m in f[\"matches\"]:\n    print(\"Lib 2019 final:\", m[\"date\"], m[\"home_team\"], m[\"home_goals\"], \"-\", m[\"away_goals\"], m[\"away_team\"])\n\n# Cup 2019 finals\ncf = queries.search_matches(repo, competition=\"Copa do Brasil\", season=2019, stage=\"final\")\nprint(\"Cup 2019 finals:\", [(m['home_team'], m['home_goals'], m['away_goals'], m['away_team']) for m in cf[\"matches\"]])\nprint(\"final_rounds:\", repo.final_rounds)\n\n# team_stats: Palmeiras competitions\nts = queries.team_stats(repo, \"Palmeiras\")\nprint(\"Palmeiras comps:\", [(c[\"competition\"], c[\"matches\"]) for c in ts[\"by_competition\"]])\n\n# find_team cross-file\nft = queries.find_team(repo, \"Atlético Mineiro\")\nprint(\"Atletico Mineiro:\", [(r[\"team\"], r[\"matches_in_dataset\"], r[\"players_in_fifa_dataset\"]) for r in ft[\"results\"]])\n\n# last Flamengo x Corinthians match\nh = queries.head_to_head(repo, \"Flamengo\", \"Corinthians\", limit=1)\nprint(\"Fla x Cor most recent:\", h[\"most_recent\"][\"date\"], h[\"most_recent\"][\"home_team\"], h[\"most_recent\"][\"home_goals\"], \"-\", h[\"most_recent\"][\"away_goals\"], h[\"most_recent\"][\"away_team\"], \"| total:\", h[\"matches_played\"])\n\n# biggest win 2019 serie a\nbw = queries.biggest_wins(repo, competition=\"Brasileirão Serie A\", season=2019, limit=3)\nfor m in bw[\"biggest_wins\"]:\n    print(\"2019 big win:\", m[\"date\"], m[\"home_team\"], m[\"home_goals\"], \"-\", m[\"away_goals\"], m[\"away_team\"])\n\n# search date range\nr = queries.search_matches(repo, date_from=\"2019-05-01\", date_to=\"2019-05-31\", competition=\"Brasileirão Serie A\", limit=1)\nprint(\"May 2019 Serie A matches:\", r[\"total_matches\"])\n\n# player position search\npl = queries.search_players(repo, club=\"Santos\", position=\"forward\", limit=10)\nprint(\"Santos forwards:\", [(p[\"name\"], p[\"overall\"]) for p in pl[\"players\"]])\npl2 = queries.search_players(repo, club=\"Gremio\", min_overall=80, limit=10)\nprint(\"Grêmio >=80:\", [(p[\"name\"], p[\"overall\"]) for p in pl2[\"players\"]])\n\n# stadium sample from 2019\nm = [x for x in repo.matches if x.season == 2019 and x.stadium and x.competition.startswith(\"Brasileirão\")][:2]\nprint(\"stadiums:\", [(x.home_display, x.stadium) for x in m])\n\n# derbies 2019 serie a\nd = queries.derby_matches(repo, season=2019)\nprint(\"derbies 2019:\", d[\"total_matches\"], [x[\"derby\"] for x in d[\"derbies\"][:5]])\n\n# rankings home win rate 2023 serie a\nrk = queries.team_rankings(repo, competition=\"serie a\", season=2023, metric=\"wins\", limit=3)\nprint(\"2023 wins:\", [(r[\"team\"], r[\"wins\"]) for r in rk[\"rankings\"]])\nEOF","timeout":120000,"workdir":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0"},"output":"Corinthians 2019: {'matches': 46, 'wins': 17, 'draws': 15, 'losses': 14, 'goals_for': 53, 'goals_against': 43, 'points': 66, 'win_rate': 0.37} | home: {'matches': 23, 'wins': 12, 'draws': 7, 'losses': 4, 'goals_for': 31, 'goals_against': 17, 'points': 43, 'win_rate': 0.522}\nLib 2019 final: 2019-11-23 Flamengo 2 - 1 River Plate\nCup 2019 finals: [('Internacional', 1, 2, 'Athletico Paranaense'), ('Athletico Paranaense', 1, 0, 'Internacional')]\nfinal_rounds: {2012: 6, 2013: 8, 2014: 8, 2015: 8, 2016: 7, 2017: 8, 2018: 8, 2019: 8, 2020: 8, 2021: 3}\nPalmeiras comps: [('Brasileirão Serie A', 725), ('Copa Libertadores', 81), ('Copa do Brasil', 72)]\nAtletico Mineiro: [('Atlético-MG', 897, 20)]\nFla x Cor most recent: 2023-10-08 Corinthians 1 - 1 Flamengo | total: 47\n2019 big win: 2019-12-05 Flamengo 6 - 1 Avai\n2019 big win: 2019-09-26 Gremio 6 - 1 Avai\n2019 big win: 2019-08-04 Santos 6 - 1 Goias\nMay 2019 Serie A matches: 50\nSantos forwards: [('Luimo Boas Santos', 79), ('Arthur Silbeira', 68), ('Fachendinho', 62)]\nGrêmio >=80: [('Josué Chiamulera', 83), ('Ronaldo Cabrais', 83), ('Raphaelito Anjos', 82)]\nstadiums: [('Sao Paulo', 'Morumbi'), ('Atlético-MG', 'Independência')]\nderbies 2019: 14 ['Clássico-Rei', 'Clássico Mineiro', 'Dérbi Campineiro', 'Derby Paulista', 'Choque-Rei']\n2023 wins: [('Gremio', 21), ('Palmeiras', 19), ('Atlético-MG', 19)]\n","metadata":{"output":"Corinthians 2019: {'matches': 46, 'wins': 17, 'draws': 15, 'losses': 14, 'goals_for': 53, 'goals_against': 43, 'points': 66, 'win_rate': 0.37} | home: {'matches': 23, 'wins': 12, 'draws': 7, 'losses': 4, 'goals_for': 31, 'goals_against': 17, 'points': 43, 'win_rate': 0.522}\nLib 2019 final: 2019-11-23 Flamengo 2 - 1 River Plate\nCup 2019 finals: [('Internacional', 1, 2, 'Athletico Paranaense'), ('Athletico Paranaense', 1, 0, 'Internacional')]\nfinal_rounds: {2012: 6, 2013: 8, 2014: 8, 2015: 8, 2016: 7, 2017: 8, 2018: 8, 2019: 8, 2020: 8, 2021: 3}\nPalmeiras comps: [('Brasileirão Serie A', 725), ('Copa Libertadores', 81), ('Copa do Brasil', 72)]\nAtletico Mineiro: [('Atlético-MG', 897, 20)]\nFla x Cor most recent: 2023-10-08 Corinthians 1 - 1 Flamengo | total: 47\n2019 big win: 2019-12-05 Flamengo 6 - 1 Avai\n2019 big win: 2019-09-26 Gremio 6 - 1 Avai\n2019 big win: 2019-08-04 Santos 6 - 1 Goias\nMay 2019 Serie A matches: 50\nSantos forwards: [('Luimo Boas Santos', 79), ('Arthur Silbeira', 68), ('Fachendinho', 62)]\nGrêmio >=80: [('Josué Chiamulera', 83), ('Ronaldo Cabrais', 83), ('Raphaelito Anjos', 82)]\nstadiums: [('Sao Paulo', 'Morumbi'), ('Atlético-MG', 'Independência')]\nderbies 2019: 14 ['Clássico-Rei', 'Clássico Mineiro', 'Dérbi Campineiro', 'Derby Paulista', 'Choque-Rei']\n2023 wins: [('Gremio', 21), ('Palmeiras', 19), ('Atlético-MG', 19)]\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0, \".\")\nfrom brazilian_soccer.repository import DataRepository\nfrom brazilian_soccer import queries\nrepo = DataRepository()\n\n# Corinthians home 2019 (complete season)\nts = queries.team_stats(repo, \"Corinthians\", season=2019)\nprint(\"Corinthians 2019:\", ts[\"overall\"], \"| home:\", ts[\"home\"])\n\n# Libertadores 2019 final\nf = queries.search_matches(repo, competition=\"Libertadores\", season=2019, stage=\"final\")\nfor m in f[\"matches\"]:\n    print(\"Lib 2019 final:\", m[\"date\"], m[\"home_team\"], m[\"home_goals\"], \"-\", m[\"away_goals\"], m[\"away_team\"])\n\n# Cup 2019 finals\ncf = queries.search_matches(repo, competition=\"Copa do Brasil\", season=2019, stage=\"final\")\nprint(\"Cup 2019 finals:\", [(m['home_team'], m['home_goals'], m['away_goals'], m['away_team']) for m in cf[\"matches\"]])\nprint(\"final_rounds:\", repo.final_rounds)\n\n# team_stats: Palmeiras competitions\nts = queries.team_stats(repo, \"Palmeiras\")\nprint(\"Palmeiras comps:\", [(c[\"competition\"], c[\"matches\"]) for c in ts[\"by_competition\"]])\n\n# find_team cross-file\nft = queries.find_team(repo, \"Atlético Mineiro\")\nprint(\"Atletico Mineiro:\", [(r[\"team\"], r[\"matches_in_dataset\"], r[\"players_in_fifa_dataset\"]) for r in ft[\"results\"]])\n\n# last Flamengo x Corinthians match\nh = queries.head_to_head(repo, \"Flamengo\", \"Corinthians\", limit=1)\nprint(\"Fla x Cor most recent:\", h[\"most_recent\"][\"date\"], h[\"most_recent\"][\"home_team\"], h[\"most_recent\"][\"home_goals\"], \"-\", h[\"most_recent\"][\"away_goals\"], h[\"most_recent\"][\"away_team\"], \"| total:\", h[\"matches_played\"])\n\n# biggest win 2019 serie a\nbw = queries.biggest_wins(repo, competition=\"Brasileirão Serie A\", season=2019, limit=3)\nfor m in bw[\"biggest_wins\"]:\n    print(\"2019 big win:\", m[\"date\"], m[\"home_team\"], m[\"home_goals\"], \"-\", m[\"away_goals\"], m[\"away_team\"])\n\n# search date range\nr = queries.search_matches(repo, date_from=\"2019-05-01\", date_to=\"2019-05-31\", competition=\"Brasileirão Serie A\", limit=1)\nprint(\"May 2019 Serie A matches:\", r[\"total_matches\"])\n\n# player position search\npl = queries.search_players(repo, club=\"Santos\", position=\"forward\", limit=10)\nprint(\"Santos forwards:\", [(p[\"name\"], p[\"overall\"]) for p in pl[\"players\"]])\npl2 = queries.search_players(repo, club=\"Gremio\", min_overall=80, limit=10)\nprint(\"Grêmio >=80:\", [(p[\"name\"], p[\"overall\"]) for p in pl2[\"players\"]])\n\n# stadium sample from 2019\nm = [x for x in repo.matches if x.season == 2019 and x.stadium and x.competition.startswith(\"Brasileirão\")][:2]\nprint(\"stadiums:\", [(x.home_display, x.stadium) for x in m])\n\n# derbies 2019 serie a\nd = queries.derby_matches(repo, season=2019)\nprint(\"derbies 2019:\", d[\"total_matches\"], [x[\"derby\"] for x in d[\"derbies\"][:5]])\n\n# rankings home win rate 2023 serie a\nrk = queries.team_rankings(repo, competition=\"serie a\", season=2023, metric=\"wins\", limit=3)\nprint(\"2023 wins:\", [(r[\"team\"], r[\"wins\"]) for r in rk[\"rankings\"]])\nEOF","time":{"start":1788238658672,"end":1788238658697}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The MCP protocol works end-to-end. Now let me write the BDD test suite. Plan:\n\n- `pytest.ini` — testpaths, utf-8\n- `tests/conftest.py` — fixtures: repo (session), mcp client (session, subprocess)\n- `tests/test_normalize.py` — name/date/value normalization BDD\n- `tests/test_match_queries.py` — match search scenarios\n- `tests/test_team_queries.py` — team stats + rankings\n- `tests/test_player_queries.py` — players\n- `tests/test_competition_queries.py` — standings, competition info\n- `tests/test_statistics.py` — h2h, biggest wins, stats summary, derbies\n- `tests/test_mcp_protocol.py` — e2e protocol tests\n- `tests/test_performance.py` — timing gates\n\nGWT structure: each test with Gherkin-style docstring at module level (Feature), and Given/When/Then comments in tests. This matches TASK.md's \"Use BDD (Behavior-Driven Development) test scenarios\" with the Gherkin examples given.\n\nLet me write conftest with a session repo fixture and an MCPClient helper class using subprocess + select with timeouts.\n\nFacts to assert (verified from dev runs):\n- 2019 Serie A: champion Flamengo, 90 pts, 28W 6D 4L, 380 matches, 20 teams ✓ spec example!\n- 2018 champion Palmeiras; 2015 Corinthians; 2021 Atlético-MG; 2003 Cruzeiro; 2012 Fluminense.\n- 2019 relegated contains Cruzeiro & CSA (also Chapecoense, Avaí).\n- 2022 partial (299 matches, data_complete False).\n- Fla-Flu h2h: 44 matches, 18 wins Flamengo, 12 Fluminense, 14 draws; total = sum.\n- Palmeiras 2023: 43 matches (37 Serie A + 6 Copa do Brasil).\n- Neymar Jr overall 92, top Brazilian. 827 Brazilian players.\n- Grêmio: 20 players. Flamengo: 0 players (not licensed in FIFA 19).\n- Gabriel Jesus at Manchester City, ST, 83.\n- Biggest wins include margin 8 (São Paulo 9-1 4 de Julho Copa do Brasil 2021; River Plate 8-0 Binacional Libertadores 2020).\n- Serie A summary: 8321 matches, avg 2.57, home win rate 0.497.\n- Copa do Brasil 1554 matches 2012-2023; Libertadores 1253 2013-2022; Serie B 3677; Serie C 1807.\n- Derbies 2023: 16.\n- Copa do Brasil finals: 2019 season final round = 8 (check final_rounds); Libertadores 2013 final: Olimpia vs Atlético-MG 2-0, 2-0.\n- search_matches Flamengo 2023: 48 matches.\n- team_rankings away_points all-time: São Paulo 387.\n- Corinthians home record 2022: compute — let me compute quickly to have expected values... Actually tests should compute expectations from the repo itself OR assert structural invariants + known facts. For \"Corinthians home record 2022\" I can assert structural: matches=19, wins+draws+losses=19, goals consistency. Plus champion facts for known values. Let me compute a couple to hardcode? Risky if I compute wrong; better assert invariants + spot-check facts I'm sure of (e.g., Corinthians 2022 home matches == 19).\n\nHmm — for the \"spec example\" fidelity: \"Corinthians home record (2022): Matches 19, Wins 11...\" — that's the spec's illustration of FORMAT, not necessarily real values. I'll assert Matches == 19 and W+D+L == 19.\n\nLet me also verify a few more test facts before writing:\n- 2022 Corinthians home matches (should be 19 — 38 rounds, half home; 2022 partial 299/380 matches → Corinthians home may be < 19! Let me use 2019 instead — complete season: Corinthians 2019 home = 19).\n- Libertadores 2019 final: Flamengo vs River Plate (Flamengo won 2-1 at home after 0-1? Actually 2019 final single match in Santiago? No wait — 2019 final was two-legged? Flamengo beat River 2-0 in the second leg in Rio (Gabo goals), first leg 0-0? No — 2019 Libertadores final was SINGLE match? No! 2019 was two-legged: River 0-2 Flamengo? Hmm. Let me just check from data rather than memory.\n- Copa do Brasil finals: e.g., 2019 final round 8; Athletico-PR won 2019 Copa do Brasil vs Internacional. Data: Cup 2019 rounds up to 8 ✓.\n\nLet me check some of these quickly, then write tests. Also — performance: repo load 1.05s; queries are ms. Performance tests trivially pass.\n\nAlso cross-file test: find_team(\"Atletico Mineiro\") == find_team(\"Atletico-MG\") entity, with both matches and players > 0. Player count for atletico mg = 20 ✓.\n\nOne more thing — I need to make sure tests work when run from the repo root with the venv pytest: `./venv/bin/python -m pytest`. The `brazilian_soccer` package must be importable: tests add rootdir to sys.path via conftest? pytest adds rootdir to sys.path automatically with rootdir conftest? Actually pytest inserts the conftest directory into sys.path (rootdir insertion happens for test collection paths with no __init__.py — \"rootdir\"-based insertion). With tests/ having no __init__.py and pytest.ini at root, running `pytest` from root: conftest.py in tests/ → tests dir added to sys.path, but the ROOT isn't automatically on sys.path unless... Actually pytest adds the conftest's parent dir. Hmm — safest: in tests/conftest.py add sys.path.insert(0, rootdir). Standard approach. Also server.py subprocess invocation uses sys.executable with cwd=repo root; server.py itself inserts its own dir into sys.path ✓.\n\nLet me check Corinthians 2019 home record and Libertadores finals from data.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b54439e001uis5oOsoorYg0D","sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","messageID":"msg_05b53ccc20014GG3HxftMNKL85"}}
