{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788238753908,"sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a83a802964a522e9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"[pytest]\ntestpaths = tests\naddopts = -ra\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/pytest.ini"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/pytest.ini","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"pytest.ini","time":{"start":1788238753901,"end":1788238753907}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting:\n- Corinthians 2019 Serie A home: 19 matches ✓ perfect for the spec-style test.\n- **2023 champion computes as Grêmio (68 pts) vs real Palmeiras (won 2023 with more points)** — the BR-Football 2023 data is partial/quirky (377 matches; and apparently missing some Palmeiras wins — real 2023: Palmeiras 82 pts, Grêmio 71). The 2023 Serie A data in BR-Football is incomplete/incorrect for standings purposes (only 377 matches and possibly missing rounds). Hmm — 68+67+66... total points seem low (real 2023: Palmeiras 82, Grêmio 71, Atlético 70? hmm close-ish but off).\n\nHmm wait — actually let me reconsider: real 2023 Brasileirão final table: 1. Palmeiras 82 (23W 13D 2L? no...). Let me recall: Palmeiras 2023: 24W 10D 4L = 82. Grêmio: 20W 11D 7L = 71. Botafogo collapsed from huge lead. Our data gives Grêmio 21-5-12=38 games?? 21+5+12=38 matches for Grêmio but 377 total... hmm Grêmio played 38 while others less? Whatever — the 2023 BR-Football data is partial (377) and slightly inaccurate. data_complete: False is flagged ✓.\n\nSo for 2023 tests: assert structure (partial flag, teams=20) NOT the champion. Good decision — test standings champion for 2019/2018/2015/2003 etc. (accurate sources) and completeness flags for 2023.\n\nNow let me write the tests. Also remove dev_check.py at the end.\n\nTest plan (~60+ assertions across 9 files):\n\n**conftest.py**:\n- `repo` session fixture\n- `mcp` session fixture: MCPClient class wrapping subprocess; methods: request(method, params, id) → response; call_tool(name, args) → parsed result; close.\n\n**test_normalize.py** (Feature: Data normalization):\n- Scenario: team name variants → same (base, qualifier): \"Palmeiras-SP\" ≡ \"Palmeiras\" ≡ \"SE Palmeiras\" ≡ \"palmeiras\"\n- Scenario: accented names: \"Grêmio\" ≡ \"Gremio-RS\" ≡ \"gremio\"\n- Scenario: full official names: \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" → corinthians; \"Atlético Paranaense\" ≡ \"Athletico-PR\" ≡ \"Atletico-PR\"; \"Atlético Mineiro\" ≡ \"Atletico-MG\"; \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" ≡ \"Vasco\"; \"Fortaleza Esporte Clube\" → fortaleza\n- Scenario: distinct clubs stay distinct: \"Botafogo-RJ\" vs \"Botafogo-PB\"; \"America-MG\" vs \"America-RN\"; \"Vitória-BA\" vs \"Vitória-ES\" (check entities exist: \"vitoria ba\", \"vitoria es\"); \"Guarani\" (SP) vs \"Guaraní-PAR\" — assert different keys\n- Scenario: international qualifier forms: \"Nacional (URU)\" ≡ \"Nacional-URU\"; \"Olimpia-PAR\" ≡ \"Olimpia\"\n- Scenario: date formats: \"2012-05-19 18:30:00\" → (date(2012,5,19), \"18:30\"); \"29/03/2003\" → (date(2003,3,29), None); \"2023-09-24\" → date\n- Scenario: numeric parsing: \"1.0\" → 1, \"NA\" → None, \"-\" → None, \"\" → None\n- Scenario: UTF-8 roundtrip: resolve \"Grêmio\", \"Avaí\", \"Fortaleza\" succeed.\n\n**test_match_queries.py** (Feature: Match queries):\n- Scenario: matches between two teams (Gherkin from TASK): head_to_head Flamengo/Fluminense → 44 matches; each match dict has date/scores/competition\n- Scenario: search_matches with team+season: Palmeiras 2023 → 43 total (cross-file: Serie A + Copa do Brasil) — assert both competitions present\n- Scenario: by competition alias: competition=\"brasileirao\" works\n- Scenario: by date range: May 2019 Serie A → 50 matches, all dates within range\n- Scenario: home_team/away_team filters: search Flamengo home vs away counts\n- Scenario: venue filter\n- Scenario: Libertadores stage filter: 2019 \"final\" → single match Flamengo 2-1 River Plate; \"quarterfinals\" 2019 → 8 matches\n- Scenario: Copa do Brasil finals 2019: two matches between Internacional and Athletico Paranaense\n- Scenario: sort order: date_asc first ≤ last\n- Scenario: limit + truncated flag\n- Scenario: last match between two teams (\"When did Flamengo last play Corinthians?\") → most_recent 2023-10-08\n- Scenario: raw source search: source=\"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\" → returns matches incl. duplicates (2021 Serie A: raw count > curated)\n- Scenario: unknown competition → QueryError\n\n**test_team_queries.py** (Feature: Team queries):\n- Scenario: team stats for one season (spec Gherkin: Palmeiras 2023 stats → wins/losses/draws/goals) — assert structure + matches count 43 consistency\n- Scenario: Corinthians home record 2019: 19 matches, W+D+L=19, GF/GA consistency (spec example \"Corinthians home record\")\n- Scenario: by-competition breakdown (Palmeiras played in 3 competitions) — spec: \"What competitions has Palmeiras played in?\"\n- Scenario: home/away splits sum to overall\n- Scenario: team_rankings best away record: metric away_points top = Sao Paulo (all-time); assert ranking structure + top has away_points ≥ others\n- Scenario: most goals in Serie A 2023: standings goals_for top — check: team_rankings goals_for 2023 serie a → top is Palmeiras? Let me compute... I'll assert from standings instead: 2023 table row goals_for sorted — I'll just assert the tool returns teams with goals_for and the max matches. Hmm — for a known fact: \"Which team scored the most goals in Serie A 2023?\" — compute expected in test via standings table max. That's circular... Instead assert structural + spot: 2019 Serie A top scorer team = Flamengo (86 GF — they had the best attack 2019 ✓ real). From dev: Flamengo 2019 goals_for 86 ✓.\n- Scenario: ambiguous team error: team_stats(\"America\") raises QueryError mentioning America-MG/America-RN\n- Scenario: find_team disambiguations\n\n**test_player_queries.py** (Feature: Player queries):\n- Scenario: Brazilian players count 827; top-rated Neymar Jr 92\n- Scenario: highest-rated at a club: Grêmio 20 players sorted by overall desc\n- Scenario: club not in FIFA data: Flamengo → 0 players (with graceful empty result)\n- Scenario: search by name: Gabriel Jesus → Manchester City ST 83\n- Scenario: player not found → QueryError (Gabriel Barbosa)\n- Scenario: position group filter: Santos forwards > 0, all position_group == forward\n- Scenario: min_overall filter: Grêmio min_overall=80 → all ≥ 80\n- Scenario: player_detail by id: Neymar id 158023 → detail with attributes\n- Scenario: cross-file join: find_team(\"Atlético Mineiro\") → same entity as Atletico-MG with matches_in_dataset > 800 and players 20 (spec cross-file requirement!)\n\n**test_competition_queries.py** (Feature: Competition queries):\n- Scenario: standings 2019 (spec Gherkin!): champion Flamengo 90 pts, 28W-6D-4L, 380 matches, 20 teams, relegated includes Cruzeiro+CSA\n- Scenario: champions across seasons: 2003 Cruzeiro, 2012 Fluminense, 2015 Corinthians, 2018 Palmeiras, 2021 Atlético-MG, 2022 Palmeiras\n- Scenario: 2022 partial data flagged (299 matches, data_complete False)\n- Scenario: 2023 partial flagged\n- Scenario: competition_info lists 5 competitions with expected season ranges (Serie A 2003-2023, Libertadores 2013-2022, Copa do Brasil 2012-2023)\n- Scenario: unknown season → QueryError with available seasons\n- Scenario: standings tie-break sorting sanity (positions ordered by points desc)\n- Scenario: Serie B 2023 champion Vitória\n\n**test_statistics.py** (Feature: Statistical analysis):\n- Scenario: avg goals Serie A ≈ 2.57 (assert 2.4 < x < 2.7) + home win rate > away win rate (known home advantage)\n- Scenario: biggest wins: top margin 8; includes Flamengo 6-1 Avai in 2019 serie a (from dev: 2019-12-05 Flamengo 6-1 Avaí — assert margin 5 in 2019 Serie A top-3)\n- Scenario: head-to-head totals consistency: wins+draws+losses == matches_played; goals consistent\n- Scenario: stats_summary season comparison 2018 vs 2019 (spec: \"Compare the 2018 and 2019 seasons\") — both summaries returned with all fields\n- Scenario: derbies in 2023 → 16 matches; derbies include named rivalries\n- Scenario: biggest win winner display\n\n**test_mcp_protocol.py** (Feature: MCP protocol):\n- initialize handshake (protocol version echo, serverInfo)\n- tools/list exposes 12 tools with inputSchema\n- tools/call returns text content JSON\n- tools/call QueryError → isError\n- unknown tool → JSON-RPC error -32602\n- ping\n- resources/list + read\n- malformed JSON → -32700\n- method not found → -32601\n- notification → no response\n- server exit clean\n\n**test_performance.py**:\n- repo load < 5s (session fixture timing — hmm, load happens once; measure in fixture? I'll time the fixture creation inside a test via fresh repo? Loading twice is 2s — fine: create fresh repo in test and time it. Assert < 5s.)\n- simple lookups < 2s: search_matches team, player search, head_to_head\n- aggregates < 5s: standings, team_rankings, stats_summary\n\n**test_repository.py** (data loading integrity):\n- all 6 files loaded, counts match (4180 rows → 4098 loaded etc.)\n- curated 16612 matches; raw 23854\n- every match has date, goals, entities resolve\n- 2019 Serie A curated = 380 with single source\n- dedup: no duplicate (competition, season, date, home, away, goals) in curated\n- stadium merge: 2019 Serie A matches with stadium == 378\n- corners merge: some 2018 Serie A matches have corners (>0)\n\nThat's comprehensive. Let me also double check the entity for \"Vitória-ES\" exists (test normalize): quals for vitoria = {ba, es} → entities \"vitoria ba\", \"vitoria es\" ✓. And \"Botafogo-PB\": entity \"botafogo pb\" — from BR-Football \"Botafogo PB\" ✓.\n\nOne more check — resolve(\"Nacional-URU\") vs \"Nacional (URU)\" → both (\"nacional\", \"uru\") → entity \"nacional uru\" ✓.\n\nAlso \"Guarani\" → alias \"guarani sp\" ✓ distinct from \"Guaraní-PAR\" → (\"guarani\",\"par\") ✓.\n\nNow — timing the repo load in a test: repo fixture is session-scoped; for load timing test, construct a NEW DataRepository (1.05s) and assert < 5s. OK.\n\nFor the MCP client fixture: subprocess with `./venv/bin/python server.py` — better: sys.executable (which will be the venv python when running under ./venv/bin/pytest ✓). cwd = repo root (Path(__file__).parent.parent). server.py inserts its dir in sys.path ✓.\n\nEdge: The MCP client must handle stderr — pipe to DEVNULL to avoid blocking.\n\nTimeouts: select-based read with 30s timeout; fail clearly.\n\nCleanup: close stdin, wait.\n\nNow — pytest.ini:\n```ini\n[pytest]\ntestpaths = tests\naddopts = -ra\n```\n\nAlso — should tests be tolerant if run with plain `pytest` (non-venv)? sys.executable = whatever python runs pytest; server.py needs no external deps ✓ stdlib only — works with any python 3.10+ (uses `X | None` unions — 3.10+; venv is 3.12 ✓).\n\nconftest sys.path: insert repo root so `import brazilian_soccer` works regardless of how pytest is invoked.\n\nLet me write all test files now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b55efa3001rH10MAwHYQoP9M","sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","messageID":"msg_05b5543a0001KhRZvj19t6US6g"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788238758402,"sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a8c6f061e500f9a9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"Shared fixtures: a loaded repository and a live MCP server process.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport select\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pytest\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n\nfrom brazilian_soccer.repository import DataRepository\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef repo() -> DataRepository:\n    return DataRepository(ROOT / \"data\" / \"kaggle\")\n\n\nclass MCPClient:\n    \"\"\"Minimal MCP stdio client driving the real server subprocess.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, process: subprocess.Popen) -> None:\n        self.process = process\n        self._next_id = 0\n\n    def send(self, payload: dict) -> None:\n        self.process.stdin.write(json.dumps(payload) + \"\\n\")\n        self.process.stdin.flush()\n\n    def read(self, timeout: float = 30.0) -> dict:\n        ready, _, _ = select.select([self.process.stdout], [], [], timeout)\n        if not ready:\n            raise TimeoutError(\"MCP server did not respond in time\")\n        line = self.process.stdout.readline()\n        if not line:\n            raise AssertionError(\"MCP server closed stdout unexpectedly\")\n        return json.loads(line)\n\n    def request(self, method: str, params: dict | None = None) -> dict:\n        self._next_id += 1\n        message = {\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": self._next_id, \"method\": method}\n        if params is not None:\n            message[\"params\"] = params\n        self.send(message)\n        response = self.read()\n        assert response.get(\"id\") == self._next_id\n        return response\n\n    def notify(self, method: str, params: dict | None = None) -> None:\n        message = {\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"method\": method}\n        if params is not None:\n            message[\"params\"] = params\n        self.send(message)\n\n    def call_tool(self, name: str, arguments: dict) -> dict:\n        response = self.request(\n            \"tools/call\", {\"name\": name, \"arguments\": arguments}\n        )\n        assert \"result\" in response, response\n        result = response[\"result\"]\n        assert result[\"content\"][0][\"type\"] == \"text\"\n        if result.get(\"isError\"):\n            raise AssertionError(f\"tool error: {result['content'][0]['text']}\")\n        return json.loads(result[\"content\"][0][\"text\"])\n\n    def close(self) -> None:\n        if self.process.stdin and not self.process.stdin.closed:\n            self.process.stdin.close()\n        self.process.wait(timeout=30)\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef mcp() -> MCPClient:\n    process = subprocess.Popen(\n        [sys.executable, str(ROOT / \"server.py\")],\n        cwd=str(ROOT),\n        stdin=subprocess.PIPE,\n        stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n        stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL,\n        text=True,\n        bufsize=1,\n    )\n    client = MCPClient(process)\n    response = client.request(\n        \"initialize\",\n        {\n            \"protocolVersion\": \"2024-11-05\",\n            \"capabilities\": {},\n            \"clientInfo\": {\"name\": \"pytest\", \"version\": \"0.0.0\"},\n        },\n    )\n    assert \"result\" in response\n    client.notify(\"notifications/initialized\")\n    yield client\n    client.close()\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/tests/conftest.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/tests/conftest.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"tests/conftest.py","time":{"start":1788238758396,"end":1788238758401}},"id":"prt_05b55f081001nGKQHwJRdxEewB","sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","messageID":"msg_05b5543a0001KhRZvj19t6US6g"}}
