p\" alias for consistency with the big clubs.\n\n   For CONSISTENCY and robustness (Palmeiras-SP vs Palmeiras-xxx future), I should add the big-club aliases for ALL the big SP/RJ/etc clubs: \"palmeiras\" → \"palmeiras sp\", \"corinthians\" → \"corinthians sp\", \"sao paulo\" → \"sao paulo sp\", \"gremio\" → \"gremio rs\", \"cruzeiro\" → \"cruzeiro mg\", \"vasco\" → \"vasco rj\", \"ceara\" → \"ceara ce\", \"bahia\" → \"bahia ba\", \"fortaleza\" → \"fortaleza ce\", \"chapecoense\" → \"chapecoense sc\", \"coritiba\" → \"coritiba pr\", \"criciuma\" → \"criciuma sc\", \"figueirense\" → \"figueirense sc\", \"avai\" → \"avai sc\", \"goias\" → \"goias go\", \"sport\" → \"sport pe\", \"parana\" → \"parana pr\", \"ponte preta\" → \"ponte preta sp\", \"juventude\" already, \"joinville\" → \"joinville sc\", \"csa\" → \"csa al\", \"cuiaba\" → \"cuiaba mt\", \"flamengo\" ✓... \n\n   Is there risk? These clubs have no same-named small club conflict, so the collapse already joins them — the alias is a no-op for entity identity. But it makes split_team deterministic and entity keys stable. Hmm — but wait: if I alias \"palmeiras\" → \"palmeiras sp\", the entity key becomes... base \"palmeiras\" quals {sp} → single → collapse → entity key \"palmeiras\" ✓ same as before. And \"Palmeiras\" bare → (\"palmeiras\",\"sp\") ✓ pair equality works.\n\n   Which big clubs NEED it (to fix pair-level tests)? \"Palmeiras\", \"Grêmio\" (\"gremio\" bare vs \"Gremio-RS\" → (\"gremio\", None) vs (\"gremio\",\"rs\")). My normalize tests assert pair identity for Palmeiras and Grêmio. Let me add the full set of big-club aliases — it's principled: bare name of a club that also appears with a known suffix → canonicalize to suffixed pair. Risk check: \"vasco\" → \"vasco rj\": any other Vasco? \"Vitória da Conquista\"? no. Fine. \"sport\" → \"sport pe\" ✓. \"bahia\" → \"bahia ba\" (Bahia de Feira is separate base ✓). \"ceara\" → \"ceara ce\". \"santos\" → \"santos sp\" already ✓.\n\n   I'll add: palmeiras, co