ity(key))} matches, variants={e.variants[:5]}\")\n\n# Flamengo 2023 h2h dates\nfrom brazilian_soccer import queries\nh = queries.head_to_head(repo, \"Flamengo\", \"Fluminense\")\nprint(\"h2h:\", h[\"matches_played\"], h[\"team_a_wins\"], \"-\", h[\"draws\"], \"-\", h[\"team_b_wins\"])\nfor m in h[\"matches\"][:6]:\n    print(\"  \", m[\"date\"], m[\"home_team\"], m[\"home_goals\"], \"-\", m[\"away_goals\"], m[\"away_team\"], m[\"competition\"], m[\"season\"], m[\"source\"])\nEOF","time":{"start":1788239013495,"end":1788239013518}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Fluminense now has 14 wins instead of 12 — so 2 more Fluminense wins appeared. Something in the last edit batch changed entity resolution slightly for Flamengo/Fluminense matches. What was in the last batch? PREFIX_TOKENS {\"se\",\"ec\",\"sc\",\"aa\"} + resolve() tightening + metric normalization. \n\nThe resolve tightening only affects resolve(), not match entity assignment. Metric fixes don't affect h2h. PREFIX_TOKENS: \"SE\"/\"EC\"/\"SC\"/\"AA\" — which raw team name in the match data starts with one of those tokens AND lost its prefix? Hmm — wait, prefix stripping happens on the CLEANED string. Are there clubs whose cleaned name starts with \"se \", \"ec \", \"sc \", \"aa \"?? \n\nOH NO. I see it!!! **\"Vasco da Gama-RJ\"** → cleaned \"vasco da gama rj\" — no. Hmm.\n\nWait — Fluminense gained 2 wins → 2 matches moved from... let me check which matches changed. Actually let me think about \"SC\" — hmm, \"SC\" doesn't appear in cleaned names... unless... hmm, Libertadores \"Nacional (SC)\"? no...\n\nLet me check empirically — diff the h2h matches vs the earlier state. Earlier: 44 matches, 18-12-14. Now: presumably still 44 matches but 14 Fluminense wins. So match SET may be same but outcome attribution changed?? That can't change from entity resolution... UNLESS team_a/team_b identity changed! If \"Flamengo\" now resolves to a DIFFERENT entity than before... e.g., bare \"Flamengo\" → alias → \"flamengo rj\" — wait, in h2h I call _resolve_one(repo, \"Flamengo\") → split_team(\"Flamengo\") → FULL alias \"flamengo\" → \"flamengo rj\" → base \"flamengo\" qual \"rj\" → resolve: qual rj → exact entity \"flamengo rj\" ✓. And Fluminense → \"fluminense rj\" ✓. \n\nHmm — unless the PREFIX strip breaks the alias! \"Flamengo\" → cleaned \"flamengo\" → prefix check: tokens[0] = \"flamengo\" not in PREFIX ✓ → alias lookup \"flamengo\" → \"flamengo rj\" ✓...\n\nHmm wait — did I possibly break something with the ALIAS \"america de natal\" addition? No...\n\nLet me look at PREFIX_TOKENS more carefully: {\"se\", \"ec\", \"sc\", \"aa\"}. Which club names could start with \"aa \"? Hmm — what about names like... \"AA\"? Hmm. Which clubs start with \"ec \"? \"EC Vitória\" → \"vitoria\" ✓ (intended). What else... \"EC Bahia\" ✓. \"SC\" — \"SC Internacional\" → \"internacional\" ✓. \"SE Palmeiras\" ✓.\n\nHmm — what about **\"SE\"**... \"SE\"? no.\n\nWait — maybe it's not PREFIX at all. Let me reconsider: h2h counts are computed from entity KEYS in matches. If some matches' home/away entity keys changed... The entity key for bare-alias'd clubs: e.g., Libertadores \"Fluminense\" → split → alias → (\"fluminense\",\"rj\") → entity key \"fluminense rj\" (qualified, since base fluminense has quals {rj, pi} → 2 quals → qualified id \"fluminense rj\"). That was TRUE BEFORE the prefix change too...\n\nHmm, hold on. Let me compare with the dev_check run output: \"Fla-Flu h2h: 44 matches, 18-12-14\" — that was run BEFORE which changes? Order of my edits:\n1. First dev run: 22 matches (entity split bug).\n2. Added bare aliases (flamengo→flamengo rj etc.) + removed int() bug... \n3. Second dev run: 44 matches, 18-12-14. ✓\n4. THEN: removed the alias re-expansion block (Bragantino bug fix)!\n5. Third dev run (tail): Fla-Flu 44 — wait did I see h2h in the third run? The tail -30 output didn't include the h2h line... Actually the third run output I saw starte