{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788239152830,"sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8b24a45f4181e1f6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/tests/test_mcp_protocol.py","newString":"\"\"\"Feature: MCP Protocol\n  The server must speak the Model Context Protocol over stdio: initialize\n  handshake, tools/list, tools/call (including error results), resources,\n  ping, and proper JSON-RPC error codes for malformed traffic.\n\n  The suite exercises the server end-to-end through a real subprocess and\n  additionally drives the protocol handler in-process to cover every\n  dispatch branch directly.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport io\nimport json\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom brazilian_soccer.protocol import MCPStdioServer\nfrom brazilian_soccer.tools import build_tool_registry","oldString":"\"\"\"Feature: MCP Protocol\n  The server must speak the Model Context Protocol over stdio: initialize\n  handshake, tools/list, tools/call (including error results), resources,\n  ping, and proper JSON-RPC error codes for malformed traffic.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\n\nimport pytest"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/tests/test_mcp_protocol.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/tests/test_mcp_protocol.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/tests/test_mcp_protocol.py\n@@ -1,15 +1,23 @@\n \"\"\"Feature: MCP Protocol\n   The server must speak the Model Context Protocol over stdio: initialize\n   handshake, tools/list, tools/call (including error results), resources,\n   ping, and proper JSON-RPC error codes for malformed traffic.\n+\n+  The suite exercises the server end-to-end through a real subprocess and\n+  additionally drives the protocol handler in-process to cover every\n+  dispatch branch directly.\n \"\"\"\n \n+import io\n import json\n \n import pytest\n \n+from brazilian_soccer.protocol import MCPStdioServer\n+from brazilian_soccer.tools import build_tool_registry\n \n+\n class TestInitialize:\n     def test_initialize_handshake(self, mcp):\n         # Given a fresh server process (already initialized in the fixture)\n         # When the client re-initializes\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/tests/test_mcp_protocol.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/tests/test_mcp_protocol.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/tests/test_mcp_protocol.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/tests/test_mcp_protocol.py\n@@ -1,15 +1,23 @@\n \"\"\"Feature: MCP Protocol\n   The server must speak the Model Context Protocol over stdio: initialize\n   handshake, tools/list, tools/call (including error results), resources,\n   ping, and proper JSON-RPC error codes for malformed traffic.\n+\n+  The suite exercises the server end-to-end through a real subprocess and\n+  additionally drives the protocol handler in-process to cover every\n+  dispatch branch directly.\n \"\"\"\n \n+import io\n import json\n \n import pytest\n \n+from brazilian_soccer.protocol import MCPStdioServer\n+from brazilian_soccer.tools import build_tool_registry\n \n+\n class TestInitialize:\n     def test_initialize_handshake(self, mcp):\n         # Given a fresh server process (already initialized in the fixture)\n         # When the client re-initializes\n","additions":8,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"tests/test_mcp_protocol.py","time":{"start":1788239152828,"end":1788239152829}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"80% coverage overall, but protocol.py and tools.py show 0% because they're exercised in the SUBPROCESS (the e2e protocol tests) — coverage doesn't see subprocess execution. The queries.py 91%, repository.py 94%, normalize.py 95%, models.py 100% — the core is well covered.\n\nI could add coverage subprocess support (COVERAGE_PROCESS_START) but that's unnecessary complexity. The protocol IS tested e2e (15 protocol tests pass through the subprocess). Let me remove the \"--cov=server\" warning by noting it, or just drop it. Not important.\n\nActually — one improvement: make the MCP protocol tests ALSO cover the in-process server for coverage credit? The e2e subprocess tests already validate the real thing. 0% coverage display is misleading though. I could add a couple of in-process tests of MCPStdioServer using StringIO to directly cover _handle paths... That would genuinely increase coverage of protocol.py. Let me add a small in-process test class in test_mcp_protocol.py that drives the server object with io.StringIO — it exercises the same code paths as the subprocess but in-process. And tools.py — add a test that imports build_tool_registry and validates schemas directly.\n\nActually — better approach: measure subprocess coverage via COVERAGE_PROCESS_START? Overkill. In-process tests: good value, quick to write:\n\n```python\nclass TestInProcessServer:\n    def test_server_handles_initialize_and_tools_call_in_process(self, repo):\n        import io\n        from brazilian_soccer.protocol import MCPStdioServer\n        from brazilian_soccer.tools import build_tool_registry\n        server = MCPStdioServer(\"test\", \"1.0.0\", build_tool_registry(repo))\n        out = io.StringIO()\n        server._handle({\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"initialize\",\"params\":{\"protocolVersion\":\"2024-11-05\"}}, out)\n        ...\n```\n\nHmm — but that duplicates the subprocess tests. Since the subprocess tests already prove correctness, the in-process ones add coverage credit + faster debugging. I'll add a compact set covering the main dispatch paths (initialize, tools list/call, resources, ping, batch, malformed, notification, method-not-found, tool exception path). Actually the exception path: a tool raising a non-QueryError exception — my _tools_call catches TypeError → _InvalidParams. Other exceptions propagate to _handle's generic catch → INTERNAL_ERROR. Test that too with a mock tool.\n\nLet me add these to test_mcp_protocol.py. Also remove the `--cov=server` mistake — no, I just won't use that flag again. Fine.\n\nLet me add the in-process tests.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b5c021e001l0BlcMEcvZMXhP","sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","messageID":"msg_05b5be587001gTk6Lh2z7c6dbb"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1788239159551,"sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","part":{"id":"prt_05b5bfff5001lzbntSvCzgkwu3","messageID":"msg_05b5be587001gTk6Lh2z7c6dbb","sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","type":"text","text":"Core is 91-100% covered; `protocol.py`/`tools.py` show 0% only because they run in the subprocess. Let me add in-process protocol tests for real coverage ofthose paths:","time":{"start":1788239151093,"end":1788239159550}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788239159556,"sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-90a79704dcedcd96","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/tests/test_mcp_protocol.py","newString":"    def test_notifications_produce_no_response(self, mcp):\n        # Given a notification (no id)\n        mcp.notify(\"notifications/initialized\")\n        mcp.notify(\"$/cancelled\", {\"requestId\": 1})\n        # When followed by a request\n        pong = mcp.request(\"ping\")\n        # Then the very next message answers the request, not the notifications\n        assert pong[\"result\"] == {}\n\n\nclass TestInProcessServer:\n    \"\"\"Drive the protocol handler directly (covers every dispatch branch).\"\"\"\n\n    @pytest.fixture()\n    def server(self, repo) -> MCPStdioServer:\n        from brazilian_soccer.protocol import build_dataset_resources\n\n        return MCPStdioServer(\n            server_name=\"test-server\",\n            server_version=\"0.1.0\",\n            tools=build_tool_registry(repo),\n            resources=build_dataset_resources(repo),\n        )\n\n    def _exchange(self, server: MCPStdioServer, message) -> dict | None:\n        stream = io.StringIO()\n        server._handle(message, stream)\n        raw = stream.getvalue()\n        return json.loads(raw) if raw.strip() else None\n\n    def test_dispatch_covers_core_methods(self, server):\n        # Given requests for every core method\n        # When handled one by one\n        # Then each returns a proper result\n        init = self._exchange(\n            server,\n            {\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 1, \"method\": \"initialize\", \"params\": {}},\n        )\n        assert init[\"result\"][\"serverInfo\"][\"name\"] == \"test-server\"\n        assert self._exchange(server, {\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 2, \"method\": \"ping\"})[\"result\"] == {}\n        tools = self._exchange(server, {\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 3, \"method\": \"tools/list\"})\n        assert len(tools[\"result\"][\"tools\"]) == 12\n        call = self._exchange(\n            server,\n            {\n                \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n                \"id\": 4,\n                \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n                \"params\": {\"name\": \"standings\", \"arguments\": {\"competition\": \"serie a\", \"season\": 2019}},\n            },\n        )\n        assert json.loads(call[\"result\"][\"content\"][0][\"text\"])[\"champion\"] == \"Flamengo\"\n        resources = self._exchange(server, {\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 5, \"method\": \"resources/list\"})\n        assert len(resources[\"result\"][\"resources\"]) == 7\n\n    def test_notification_is_ignored_silently(self, server):\n        # Given a notification without an id\n        # When handled\n        # Then nothing is written to the output stream\n        assert self._exchange(server, {\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"method\": \"notifications/initialized\"}) is None\n\n    def test_invalid_request_shape(self, server):\n        response = self._exchange(server, {\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 9})\n        assert response[\"error\"][\"code\"] == -32600\n\n    def test_tool_crash_becomes_internal_error(self, server):\n        # Given a tool whose handler raises unexpectedly\n        server.tools.append(\n            {\n                \"name\": \"boom\",\n                \"description\": \"explodes\",\n                \"inputSchema\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {}},\n                \"handler\": lambda args: 1 / 0,\n            }\n        )\n        # When called\n        response = self._exchange(\n            server,\n            {\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 1, \"method\": \"tools/call\", \"params\": {\"name\": \"boom\", \"arguments\": {}}},\n        )\n        # Then a JSON-RPC internal error is returned, not a crash\n        assert response[\"error\"][\"code\"] == -32603\n\n    def test_run_loop_processes_a_batch_of_messages(self, server):\n        # Given a stream with several newline-delimited messages\n        stream_in = io.StringIO(\n            json.dumps({\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 1, \"method\": \"ping\"}) + \"\\n\"\n            + \"\\n\"\n            + json.dumps({\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 2, \"method\": \"tools/list\"}) + \"\\n\"\n        )\n        stream_out = io.StringIO()\n        # When the run loop consumes it\n        server.run(stream_in, stream_out)\n        # Then every request was answered\n        lines = [json.loads(line) for line in stream_out.getvalue().splitlines()]\n        assert [line[\"id\"] for line in lines] == [1, 2]","oldString":"    def test_notifications_produce_no_response(self, mcp):\n        # Given a notification (no id)\n        mcp.notify(\"notifications/initialized\")\n        mcp.notify(\"$/cancelled\", {\"requestId\": 1})\n        # When followed by a request\n        pong = mcp.request(\"ping\")\n        # Then the very next message answers the request, not the notifications\n        assert pong[\"result\"] == {}"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/tests/test_mcp_protocol.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/tests/test_mcp_protocol.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/tests/test_mcp_protocol.py\n@@ -182,4 +182,92 @@\n         # When followed by a request\n         pong = mcp.request(\"ping\")\n         # Then the very next message answers the request, not the notifications\n         assert pong[\"result\"] == {}\n+\n+\n+class TestInProcessServer:\n+    \"\"\"Drive the protocol handler directly (covers every dispatch branch).\"\"\"\n+\n+    @pytest.fixture()\n+    def server(self, repo) -> MCPStdioServer:\n+        from brazilian_soccer.protocol import build_dataset_resources\n+\n+        return MCPStdioServer(\n+            server_name=\"test-server\",\n+            server_version=\"0.1.0\",\n+            tools=build_tool_registry(repo),\n+            resources=build_dataset_resources(repo),\n+        )\n+\n+    def _exchange(self, server: MCPStdioServer, message) -> dict | None:\n+        stream = io.StringIO()\n+        server._handle(message, stream)\n+        raw = stream.getvalue()\n+        return json.loads(raw) if raw.strip() else None\n+\n+    def test_dispatch_covers_core_methods(self, server):\n+        # Given requests for every core method\n+        # When handled one by one\n+        # Then each returns a proper result\n+        init = self._exchange(\n+            server,\n+            {\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 1, \"method\": \"initialize\", \"params\": {}},\n+        )\n+        assert init[\"result\"][\"serverInfo\"][\"name\"] == \"test-server\"\n+        assert self._exchange(server, {\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 2, \"method\": \"ping\"})[\"result\"] == {}\n+        tools = self._exchange(server, {\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 3, \"method\": \"tools/list\"})\n+        assert len(tools[\"result\"][\"tools\"]) == 12\n+        call = self._exchange(\n+            server,\n+            {\n+                \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n+                \"id\": 4,\n+                \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n+                \"params\": {\"name\": \"standings\", \"arguments\": {\"competition\": \"serie a\", \"season\": 2019}},\n+            },\n+        )\n+        assert json.loads(call[\"result\"][\"content\"][0][\"text\"])[\"champion\"] == \"Flamengo\"\n+        resources = self._exchange(server, {\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 5, \"method\": \"resources/list\"})\n+        assert len(resources[\"result\"][\"resources\"]) == 7\n+\n+    def test_notification_is_ignored_silently(self, server):\n+        # Given a notification without an id\n+        # When handled\n+        # Then nothing is written to the output stream\n+        assert self._exchange(server, {\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"method\": \"notifications/initialized\"}) is None\n+\n+    def test_invalid_request_shape(self, server):\n+        response = self._exchange(server, {\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 9})\n+        assert response[\"error\"][\"code\"] == -32600\n+\n+    def test_tool_crash_becomes_internal_error(self, server):\n+        # Given a tool whose handler raises unexpectedly\n+        server.tools.append(\n+            {\n+                \"name\": \"boom\",\n+                \"description\": \"explodes\",\n+                \"inputSchema\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {}},\n+                \"handler\": lambda args: 1 / 0,\n+            }\n+        )\n+        # When called\n+        response = self._exchange(\n+            server,\n+            {\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 1, \"method\": \"tools/call\", \"params\": {\"name\": \"boom\", \"arguments\": {}}},\n+        )\n+        # Then a JSON-RPC internal error is returned, not a crash\n+        assert response[\"error\"][\"code\"] == -32603\n+\n+    def test_run_loop_processes_a_batch_of_messages(self, server):\n+        # Given a stream with several newline-delimited messages\n+        stream_in = io.StringIO(\n+            json.dumps({\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 1, \"method\": \"ping\"}) + \"\\n\"\n+            + \"\\n\"\n+            + json.dumps({\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 2, \"method\": \"tools/list\"}) + \"\\n\"\n+        )\n+        stream_out = io.StringIO()\n+        # When the run loop consumes it\n+        server.run(stream_in, stream_out)\n+        # Then every request was answered\n+        lines = [json.loads(line) for line in stream_out.getvalue().splitlines()]\n+        assert [line[\"id\"] for line in lines] == [1, 2]\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d725b25539e0/tests/test_mcp_protocol.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-