{"type":"text","timestamp":1788239245024,"sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","part":{"id":"prt_05b5d5dc0001qIkdMfv0l8eAam","messageID":"msg_05b5d517d001uuBr7MfO4JgVZS","sessionID":"ses_fa4ccb140ffeDOyFhEFIFiRBUT","type":"text","text":"Implementation complete. All 130 tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Brazilian Soccer MCP Server** — implemented per TASK.md, stdlib-only Python (zero dependencies), speaking MCP over stdio (JSON-RPC 2.0: `initialize`, `ping`, `tools/list|call`, `resources/list|read`, batch + error codes).\n\n**Architecture** (each file opens with a context-block docstring):\n- `server.py` — entry point + `--list-tools` / `--invoke` test modes\n- `brazilian_soccer/normalize.py` — team/date/number normalization (the data-quality core)\n- `brazilian_soccer/models.py` — `Match`/`Player`/`TeamEntity`\n- `brazilian_soccer/repository.py` — loads all 6 CSVs, resolves entities, dedupes, merges stats\n- `brazilian_soccer/queries.py` — 12 tools: match search (team/opponent/date/competition/season/stage/round/source), head-to-head, team stats, rankings, find_team, player search/detail, standings, competition info, biggest wins, stats summaries, derbies\n- `tests/` — 130 BDD Given/When/Then tests across 9 suites\n\n**Key engineering decisions**:\n- **Entity resolution** — every spelling (\"Palmeiras-SP\" / \"SE Palmeiras\" / \"Grêmio\" / \"Athletico-PR\" / \"Nacional (URU)\") folds to a stable identity; same-name clubs stay distinct via state (`America-MG` vs `America-RN`), and big clubs are pinned so small namesakes (`Flamengo-PI` in Serie C) can't split or pollute records\n- **Deduplication** — 3 files overlap for 2012-2019 Serie A; per (competition, season) one preferred source is kept (23,854 raw → 16,612 curated matches) while corners/shots/stadiums from demoted sources are merged in; raw rows remain queryable via `source=`\n- **Reality-verified** — computed standings reproduce known champions (2003, 2012, 2015, 2018, 2019, 2021, 2022), the real 2019 relegation zone, and the spec's exact example table (Flamengo 90 pts, 28W-6D-4L); partial seasons (2022/2023) are flagged, not hidden\n- **Performance** — ~1s cold load, all queries in milliseconds (gates: <2s simple / <5s aggregate)\n\n**Honest data limits surfaced**: FIFA 19 has only 15 licensed Brazilian clubs (no Flamengo squad; Gabriel Barbosa absent → clear error), and Brazilian-league player names are pseudonyms.","time":{"start":1788239240640,"end":1788239245022}}}
